## Instruction
Fix-round 23 for 024B-extras-1 — CI blocker surfaced when PR was opened. `policy-check / scp/policy-check` is REQUIRED on main + failing. Root cause: conftest tries to parse review-archive JSON files in `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r*-archive/r1-*.json` as policy input data, which fails because they contain Claude Code SDK output (`{"is_error": false, "result": "..."}`) with markdown-wrapped JSON in the `result` field — not valid policy data.

**Failure message:**
```
Error: running test: parse configurations: parser unmarshal: unmarshal json:
invalid character 'u' after top-level value, path:
docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r18-archive/r1-safety_bypass.json
```

This is the SAME class of issue closed for `tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` paths in WP-SCP-022 020Q (closes TF-006) — namely, files that conftest CAN parse syntactically (JSON) but should NOT be policy-evaluated because they exist for a different purpose. Review-archive JSON files are governance artifacts (Sonnet R1 lens output), not policy data.

## FIX

In `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh`, in the target-selection loop (around line 180-200 where `tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` is already excluded), add a case for `docs/reviews/*` paths. Pattern mirror:

```bash
    case "$target" in
      tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*)
        if [ "${GITHUB_ACTIONS:-}" = "true" ]; then
          printf '::debug::skipping %s: conflict-gate fixture (audited by pytest layer, closes 020Q)\n' "$target"
        fi
        continue
        ;;
      docs/reviews/*)
        if [ "${GITHUB_ACTIONS:-}" = "true" ]; then
          printf '::debug::skipping %s: governance review artifact (Claude SDK output / dispatch package), not policy input\n' "$target"
        fi
        continue
        ;;
    esac
```

Why `docs/reviews/*` (broad) and not `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/*` (narrow):
- The pattern matches review-archive JSONs across all WP-SCP-NNN review directories (consistent with existing usage at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/` + `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/`)
- These directories are governance artifacts by convention — none of them are intended as policy data
- A narrower pattern would force per-WP exception entries; the broad pattern is the canonical SCP convention

