de is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure, and 024B-core now warns on post-v1.2.0 SHAs while keeping the v1.0.0 pin as the operational fallback until TF-023E-002 closes. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\\n\\n## Today's chain (2026-05-09 — D-035-rules retired + WP-SCP-025 parked)\\n\\n**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** the 6 D-035-aligned rules previously framed as gating CT Wave 1 entry on 2026-05-15 are **RETIRED under that deadline** — re-scoped under WP-SCP-025 (parked, post-WP-SCP-024 Threshold A). The retirement is conditional on a strategic reframe: SCP's near-term credibility depends on shipping 2-3 high-value domain rules that catch things review misses + measurable adopter consumption (≥3 cohort adopters running ≥2 SCP-R-005+ rules with ≥80% pass rate over ≥4-week observation window), not on forcing the 6 SDK-discipline rules through under deadline pressure when (a) CT D-035 Phase 5 already shipped 2026-05-07 without these rules as preconditions; (b) WP-SCP-024 cascade is operator-decided FLA-independent per 2026-05-03 §2 invariants row 4; (c) none of the 6 had been drafted with 6 days remaining; (d) parallel work on slice 024B (the actual cascade gate per plan-doc §6) would have been diluted.\\n\\n**The 6 retired rule names** (preserved here for traceability — re-evaluate at WP-SCP-025 kickoff against the §4 candidate list in the parked plan-doc):\\n1. `sdk_version_pin` (was Wave 1 gate)\\n2. `ct_sdk_conformance` (was Wave 1 gate)\\n3. `sdk_migration_waiver` (was Wave 1 gate)\\n4. `sdk_adoption_schedule` (was Wave 1 mid)\\n5. `bff_refresh_hardening` (was Wave 2 gate)\\n6. `ct_auth_provider_memoization` (was Wave 3 gate)\\n\\n**Cross-project reconciliation:** SCP filed `SCP-D035-RULES-RETIRED-2026-05-09.md` to CT governance notifications log requesting CT amendments to (a) `docs/briefings/recommender-shopify-j1-rbac-response-2026-05-09.md` Q6+Q8 to drop the 6-rules / 2026-05-15-deadline framing before the response ships, (b) `docs/plans/PLAN-CT-D-rollout.md` §3 WP-D-SCP entry to point at WP-SCP-025 backlog. CT-owned changes; SCP requesting explicitly so cross-project view stays consistent.\\n\\n**Forward work:** WP-SCP-025 (`docs/plans/WP-SCP-025-domain-rules-v1.md`) parked with 5 candidate rules (protected_tables_updated_with_migration / r1_evidence_linked_in_pr_body / waiver_expiry_within_window / secrets_not_in_committed_env_files / permission_schema_registered_within_wave_window) for WP-SCP-025 owner to review and pick 2-3 from at scoping time. Owner: TBD (named at parked-plan kickoff post-024 Threshold A).\\n\\n**Slice 024B-core remains the immediate work** — hard predecessor for cohort onboarding 024C-F per WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §6. Scope: scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + tests; 024B-extras deferred.\\n\\n## Today's chain (2026-05-09 PM — slice 024B-core + scope-split decision)\\n\\n**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** WP-SCP-024 slice 024B split into 024B-core (scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + cascade-status CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (`--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Empirical justification: original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code; R6 missed a primary deliverable; R7 fix in