2; **defers TF-023C-001 → TF-023E-001 + TF-023E-002**). NEW `docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md` (status: `not-yet-signed`) — 8-criterion checklist for operator sign-off when ≥3 adopters (FLA mandatory) opted in + first weekly aggregator clean. Closed TF-023D-003: `_log_tool_invocation` now reads active key_id from `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` via new `_resolve_audit_key_id()` helper (graceful fallback `key-ring-unreadable` if key ring empty/malformed; never blocks tool calls). Updated `test_stdio_handshake.py` expected tools list to include `consult_scorecard`. 86/86 MCP tests pass. **fix-round-3:** Two real CI gaps surfaced — (1) SCP-self opt-in attempted then reverted because GitHub blocks `actions/attest-build-provenance` on user-owned private repos (filed TF-023E-001). (2) Wrapper SHA pin bump (v1.0.0 → @5ff2acd) reverted because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation), and the `attest-scorecard` job's `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` exceed the wrapper's ceiling — startup_failure even with `scorecard-emit: false` (filed TF-023E-002 — restructure policy-check.yml so attest-scorecard is a separate top-level workflow file). USER-GATE-D criterion (i) updated: SCP-self carve-out — satisfied set is now `FLA + ≥2 of {PIM / recommender / mapp-doc-agent / control-tower}`. R1/R2 adversarial review missed both constraints (only visible at actual CI runtime in this repo's specific visibility/ownership context). Wrapper stays pinned at v1.0.0 (@41a5299) until TF-023E-002 closes. Merged at `295e0da`. |\\n| 6 | #102 | **024A** | WP-SCP-024 plan-doc v0.1 — estate cascade. Defines adopter cohort `{pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower}` (per D-035) explicitly **FLA-independent** per operator direction; canary-first sequencing PIM → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure, and 024B-core now warns on post-v1.2.0 SHAs while keeping the v1.0.0 pin as the operational fallback until TF-023E-002 closes. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\\n\\n## Today's chain (2026-05-09 — D-035-rules retired + WP-SCP-025 parked)\\n\\n**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** the 6 D-035-aligned rules previously framed as gating CT Wave 1 entry on 2026-05-15 are **RETIRED under that deadline** — re-scoped under WP-SCP-025 (parked, post-WP-SCP-024 Threshold A). The retirement is conditional on a strategic reframe: SCP's near-term credibility depends on shipping 2-3 high-value domain rules that catch things review misses + measurable adopter consumption (≥3 cohort adopters running ≥2 SCP-R-005+ rules with ≥80% pass rate over ≥4-week observation window), not on forcing the 6 SDK-discipline rules through under deadline pressure when (a) CT D-035 Phase 5 already shipped 2026-05-07 without these rules as preconditions; (b) WP-SCP-024 cascade is operator-decided FLA-independent per 2026-05-03 §2 invariants row 4; (c) none of the 6 had been drafted with 6 days remaining; (d) parallel work on slice 024B (the actual cascade gate per plan-doc §6) would have been diluted.\\n\\n**The 6 retired rule names** (preserved here for traceability — re-evaluate at WP-SCP-025 kickoff against the §4 candidate list in the parked plan-doc):\\n1. `sdk_version_pin` (was Wave 1 gate)\\n2. `ct_sdk_conformance` (was Wave 1 gate)\\n3. `sdk_migration_waiver` (was Wave 1 gate)\\n4. `sdk_adoption_schedule` (was Wave 1 mid)\\n5. `bff_refresh_hardening` (was Wave 2 gate)\\n6. `ct_auth_provider_memoization` (was Wave 3 gate)\\n\\n**Cross-project reconciliation:** SCP filed `SCP-D035-RULES-RETIRED-2026-05-09.md` to CT governance notifications log requesting CT amendments to (a) `docs/briefings/recommender-shopify-j1-rbac-response-2026-05-09.md` Q6+Q8 to drop the 6-rules / 2026-05-15-deadline framing before the response ships, (b) `docs/plans/PLAN-CT-D-rollout.md` §3 WP-D-SCP entry to point at WP-SCP-025 backlog. CT-owned changes; SCP requesting explicitly so cross-project view stays consistent.\\n\\n**Forward work:** WP-SCP-025 (`docs/plans/WP-SCP-025-domain-rules-v1.md`) parked with 5 candidate rules (protected_tables_updated_with_migration / r1_evidence_linked_in_pr_body / waiver_expiry_within_window / secrets_not_in_committed_env_files / permission_schema_registered_within_wave_window) for WP-SCP-025 owner to review and pick 2-3 from at scoping time. Owner: TBD (named at parked-plan kickoff post-024 Threshold A).\\n\\n**Slice 024B-core remains the immediate work** — hard predecessor for cohort onboarding 024C-F per WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §6. Scope: scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + tests; 024B-extras deferred.\\n\\n## Today's chain (2026-05-09 PM — slice 024B-core + scope-split decision)\\n\\n**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** WP-SCP-024 slice 024B split into 024B-core (scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + cascade-status CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (`--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Empirical justification: original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code; R6 missed a primary deliverable; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR. Surface-area-too-large for single-pass convergence. Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope — both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens.\\n\\nOriginal 024B work preserved at branch `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` (pushed to origin 2026-05-09; audit trail intact: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log + 7 R-round archive dirs).\\n\\n| # | Outcome |\\n|---|---|\\n| 1 | Slice 024B-core: `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` + `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` + `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` (CLI) + `tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh` + `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` (cascade-status enforcement only). D-044 filed scoped to core. Branch: `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-core`. |\\n| 2 | Slice 024B-extras: deferred. Scope: `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` + step 7 operator-interactive `--restore` round-trip demo. To be branched from merged 024B-core. R8-CORR-001/002/003 (extras-parking r8-archive) carry forward as known findings. |\\n| 3 | Plan-doc §6 amendment: 024C entry now conditional on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merged + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure (was: 024B + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure). Cohort cascade gate unchanged in posture; precondition list extended for clarity. |\\n\\n## Today's chain (2026-05-10 — slice 024B-extras)\\n\\n| # | Outcome |\\n|---|---|\\n| 1 | Slice 024B-extras: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore` added with GET-shape → PUT-shape transform, posture-degradation acknowledgements, required-signatures sub-resource handling, and forward-mode safety checks (path-pinned workflow lookup, no branch filter on runs API, release-tag SHA validation, working-tree prior-entry detection). |\\n| 2 | NEW `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` added with `paths: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` + `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` + `STATUS.md`; tooling slices still short-circuit in the job body. |\\n| 3 | ADOPT-001 gained §12.8 break-glass procedure; D-047 filed; DISPATCH-NOTE finalised ACTIVE. |\\n| 4 | Step-7 operator-interactive demo evidence is still operator-run; placeholder path recorded at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md`; `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` may be deleted once both 024B-core and 024B-extras merge. |\\n\\n## Open PRs (post-Threshold-A session close-out)\\n\\n- **PR #59** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/deliberate-violation-pre`; permanent fixture; CI=FAIL by design (deny); blocked structurally by required-check.\\n- **PR #67** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/waived-violation`; permanent fixture; CI=PASS via waiver suppression; label-only protection (TF-020H4-002 covers).\\n- **PR #81** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/rule-config-disabled`; permanent fixture; CI=PASS via rule-config suppression; label-only protection (TF-020H4-002 covers).\\n- **Dependabot PRs**: ✅ all 4 stale MAJOR-version Action bumps cleared 2026-05-02. setup-python (#72), upload-artifact (#44), download-artifact (#42), checkout (#43) — all merged after CI-green verification on rebased branches.\\n\\n## Open scheduled follow-ups\\n\\n| Item | Date | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| D-021 atomic workday filing (D-021 reservation) | 2026-05-31 | docs/DECISIONS.md header |\\n| Phase 2 X-CT-Timestamp activation notice (60-day advance) | 2026-07-02 | project_scheduled_followups.md item 3 |\\n| WP-SCP-019 D-019 mode.bearer_legacy operational close | 2026-09-30 | project_d019_option_b_slide |\\n| 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers TWO independent items: (1) WP-SCP-020 020K bus-factor-1 escalation (CODEOWNERS / break-glass); (2) TF-020G-001 (interactive-confirm review on adopter helper). Both items reach the same date by separate paths but are evaluated independently. | 2026-07-21 | docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md §8 + docs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020g/DISPATCH-NOTE.md |\\n| Branch-protection quarterly review (bus-factor-1; covers `v*` ruleset, `main` protection, AND `renovate/v*` ruleset) | 2026-07-30 | docs/security/branch-protection.md |\\n| WP-SCP-023 Threshold A operator sign-off — `docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md` lands as `not-yet-signed` at slice 023E; signs when ≥3 adopters opted in + ≥1 weekly aggregator clean. Operator-driven; no fixed date. | tbd | docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md |\\n\\n## Tracked-forward items from 020C.1\\n\\n- ~~**TF-005**: structural enforcement of expired rule-config at release-tag time~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020H.3** (this PR's branch); `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` refuses a tag-cut when `.scp/rule-config.yaml` (SCP-self) has any `disable: true` entry with `expires_at < <tag-cut date>`. Adopter-side rule-config expiry is enforced separately at PR time via SCP-E007.\\n- ~~**TF-006**~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020Q** (this PR) — `tests/conflict_gate/test_conflict_gate.py` gains Python-side mirrors of `policies/scp_common.rego` suppression helpers (`_scp_active_waiver_for`, `_scp_waiver_expired`, `_scp_rule_config_disabled`, `_parse_dateish_ns`); `_run_opa` detects sibling `waivers.json` + `.scp/rule-config.yaml` and passes via `--data`; 5 new fixtures land — SCP-R-001/{waiver-suppressed, waiver-expired, rule-config-disabled} + SCP-R-002/waiver-suppressed + SCP-R-004/waiver-suppressed. All 11 fixtures pass; both engines agree on every code path. Finding-id-level matching deferred to WP-SCP-023 per scp_common.rego comment. Closes the WP-SCP-023 prerequisite gate.\\n- **TF-007**: re-tighten `gh attestation verify` to hard-fail when OPA upstream begins publishing Sigstore attestations. **Extended in 020H.2** to also wire a Regal Sigstore soft-warn at re-tightening time — Regal is published via OPA's pipeline and almost certainly shares the same upstream attestation gap timeline; symmetric treatment when the gap closes. Conftest also covered (no published attestations either).\\n- **TF-008**: path-scope SCP-R-002 to waivers.json files only (currently narrowed to null/string-rooted detection only) → v1.1.\\n- **TF-024B-core-WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001**: 024B-extras workflow wiring will hardcode `--tooling-slice-id` per workflow file and omit `--allow-not-applicable` from cohort workflows, closing the residual operator-supplied slice-id bypass surface. 024B-core keeps the CLI guard + documentation only.\\n\\n## Tracked-forward items from 020D1 (closed in 020H part 3)\\n\\n- **TF-D1-001**: WP-SCP-020 §4 020H part 3 canonical adopter template repo name uses trailing dash (`standards-control-plane-`) — ✅ closed in **020H part 3** (this PR's branch); §12.7.1 + §12.7.2 use the correct repo name.\\n- **TF-D1-002**: Document fork-PR refusal as mandatory or optional for adopters — ✅ closed in **020H part 3**; §12.7.1 documents the `if:` as **mandatory** with security rationale.\\n- **TF-D1-003**: Wrapper header references 'ADOPT-001 §12' federation appendix — ✅ closed in **020H part 3**; §12.7 federation-primitive adopter integration appendix now exists.\\n\\n## Tracked-forward items from 020H part 3\\n\\n- **TF-020H3-001**: Regal binary SHA256 verification — ✅ **closed in slice 020H.2 (this PR's branch)** before the 2026-05-14 deadline. `scripts/.tool-versions` now pins `regal 0.40.0`; `scripts/scp-policy-check.lock` carries Regal SHA256 entries for all four platforms (linux-x64, linux-arm64, darwin-arm64, darwin-x64); `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` reads `REGAL_VERSION` from tool-versions, `REGAL_SHA256` from the lockfile, and resolves Regal via the new `resolve_regal()` helper symmetric with `resolve_opa()` (vendor-fallback parity). Sigstore attestation soft-warn for Regal not added (folds into TF-007).\\n- **TF-020H3-002**: ADOPT-001 §12.7 lacks an explicit \\\"do these in this order\\\" adopter onboarding sequence (was R1 completeness COMP-MIN-001). Document order implicitly encodes §12.7.1 → §12.7.2 → §12.7.3 → §12.7.4 setup flow, but a v1.1 §12.7 preamble would make the sequence explicit. No deadline (cosmetic).\\n- ~~**TF-020H3-003**: Plan §4 020H part 3 canonical YAML wrapper text uses `standards-control-plane` (no trailing dash) in two places~~ ✅ **closed opportunistically in slice 020M** (this PR's branch). Slice 020M is a plan-touch slice (it amends `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` for the typo fix itself), satisfying the TF-020H3-003 closure path. **All three lines corrected** across **two logical locations** in the plan: (1) §4 020F `extends:` shorthand `github>jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-//renovate/default#<tag>` (trailing dash added in 1 line); (2) §4 020H part 3 canonical YAML wrapper renovate marker `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-` (trailing dash added in 1 line) + reusable-workflow ref `uses: jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<commit-SHA>` (trailing dash added in 1 line). The TF's original phrasing \\\"in two places\\\" referred to the two logical locations (020F + 020H part 3); the actual character-count is three line-edits.\\n- **TF-020H3-004**: §12.7.4 path examples (`services.yml`, `output/findings/waivers.json`, `policies/**`) are SCP-internal naming (was R1 completeness COMP-NIT-001). Estate-cascade adopters (FLA, PIM, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower per WP-SCP-024) may have different file-shape conventions; v1.1 §12.7 wording could generalise. No deadline (cosmetic).\\n- **TF-020H3-005**: §12.7.2 doesn't include a one-sentence rationale for why `renovate/v*` is independent of the federation-primitive `v*` tag series (was R1 completeness COMP-NIT-002). Closure: v1.1 ADOPT-001 maintenance pass. No deadline (cosmetic).\\n\\n## Tracked-forward items from 020H.1\\n\\n- ~~**TF-020H1-001**: `enforce_release_gate` workflow~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020H.3** (this PR's branch); `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` reads `policies/deprecations.yaml` (validated against `schemas/deprecations.schema.json`) and refuses a tag-cut on `push: tags: ['v*']` when any entry's `target_release` matches the candidate AND `announced_release` is not at least one MINOR behind. `workflow_dispatch:` with `dry_run_tag` input lets the operator test before pushing. Annotation: `SCP-EREL-001`.\\n- **TF-020H1-002**: `canary-replay.yml` paging rotation — at v1.0.0 the auto-opened `rule-regression` issue assigns `@jrnb2024` only (single-operator per D-031). For estate cascade (WP-SCP-024) a paging rotation would replace the assignee-only signal. Closure path: revisit at WP-SCP-024 planning OR at the 2026-07-21 quarterly bus-factor review when a second maintainer onboards. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.1 R1 completeness COMP-MAJ-002 closure.\\n- **TF-020H1-003**: `auto-defer` GitHub Action for stale rule-proposals — currently a manual close + `defer` label step (per `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/README.md` §Process step 2). For estate scale (post-WP-SCP-024 cascade) when proposal volume warrants automation, a scheduled GH Action would close PRs with no approvals after the 48h window. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.1 R1 completeness COMP-MIN-004 closure.\\n- ~~**TF-020H1-004**: rule-config disable canary missing~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020H.4** (this PR's branch). New `canary/rule-config-disabled` branch (PR #81 DO-NOT-MERGE; SHA `841d350`) carries the deliberate SCP-R-001 violation + a `.scp/rule-config.yaml` disable entry; workflow run `25211284467` verified PASS (deny suppressed by rule-config code path; findings=0; waivers=0; disabled_rules=2). `scripts/replay-canary.sh` registry extended with `rule-config-disabled|canary/rule-config-disabled|SUCCESS|0|0`. `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/canary-evidence.md` extended with Canary 4 baseline section. Suppression-path coverage triad complete: deny / waiver-suppressed / rule-config-suppressed.\\n- ~~**TF-020H1-005**~~ ✅ primary deliverable closed in 020H.1 fix-round-1 (SAFE-nit-008): `RULE-TEMPLATE.md` §10 `[BLOCKING]` / `[deferrable]` question-marking guidance + no-quorum-with-unresolved-`[BLOCKING]` invariant landed. This TF remains nominally open only for any subsequent §10 enhancement (e.g. an auto-detect linter that flags unresolved `[BLOCKING]` markers in a proposal PR). No deadline (cosmetic).\\n\\n## Tracked-forward items from 020H.3 (release-gate)\\n\\n- **TF-020H3rg-001**: PR-time deprecation-announcement linter — currently a rule-deprecation PR adds an entry to `policies/deprecations.yaml` per the rule-RFC process; no automated check that the entry is added when a `deprecated` annotation is introduced. Closure path: a future linter step in `policy-check.yml` (or a separate workflow) that greps for new `deprecated` warning emissions in a PR diff and refuses the PR if no corresponding `policies/deprecations.yaml` entry was added in the same PR. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.3 R1 completeness COMP-MIN-002 closure.\\n- ~~**TF-020H3rg-002**: `pip install --require-hashes` for `policy-check.yml` + `release-gate.yml` pyyaml/jsonschema installs.~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020M** (this PR's branch). `requirements/policy-check.in` (top-level pins) + `requirements/policy-check.txt` (generated by `pip-compile --generate-hashes`, full transitive closure with all-platform wheel SHA256s) added. All 5 install sites (4× `policy-check.yml` + 1× `release-gate.yml`) switched to `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/policy-check.txt`. Top-level pins unchanged from v1.0.0 (`pyyaml==6.0.2` + `jsonschema==4.23.0`); only the install mechanism is hardened. PATCH bump v1.0.0 → v1.0.1 per VERSIONING.md \\\"internal refactors\\\". D-038 filed.\\n- ~~**TF-020H3rg-003**: Auto-open `release-gate-violation` issue on push:tags failure~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020H.3.1** (this PR's branch). `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` split into two jobs: `release-gate` (evaluation; `contents: read`) + `release-gate-violation-issue` (`needs: release-gate`; `if: needs.release-gate.result == 'failure' && github.event_name == 'push'`; `permissions: { contents: read, issues: write }`; pre-creates labels via `gh label create --force`; de-dups by tag substring; uses Python templating in both new-issue and comment branches). Ratified by **D-037** (issues:write job-level scope). Forward-compat assignee env: `SCP_RELEASE_GATE_ASSIGNEES` (defaults to `jrnb2024`).\\n- **TF-020H3rg-004**: Issue auto-close on corrective tag-cut — when the operator cuts the corrected `v<X>.<Y+1>.0`, the open `release-gate-violation` issue isn't auto-closed. Operator closes manually after the triage checklist completes. Closure path: a future workflow step that detects the corrected tag-cut and `gh issue close`s any open release-gate-violation issue for the bad tag-series. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.3.1 R1 completeness COMP-MIN-001 closure.\\n\\n## Tracked-forward items from 020M (supply-chain hash-pinning)\\n\\n- ~~**TF-020M-001**: `conflict-gate.yml` retains `pip install pyyaml>=6.0` (line ~42) without hash-pinning.~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020N** (this PR's branch). `requirements/conflict-gate.in` (top-level pins matching `pyproject.toml` `[project.dependencies]` + `[project.optional-dependencies.dev]`) + `requirements/conflict-gate.txt` (generated by `pip-compile --generate-hashes` under Python 3.12, full transitive closure with all-platform wheel SHA256s) added. `.github/workflows/conflict-gate.yml` \\\"Install Python dependencies\\\" step restructured to: (i) hash-pinned `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/conflict-gate.txt`; (ii) local vendored `ct-auth` wheel installed `--no-deps`; (iii) editable local SCP package installed `--no-deps`; (iv) post-install version-pin assertion (mirrors 020M SAFE-MAJ-002 pattern). No semver bump (conflict-gate is internal-only per VERSIONING.md §\\\"Scope\\\"). D-039 filed.\\n- ~~**TF-020M-002**: ADOPT-001 §12.7.13 lockfile regeneration procedure does not warn that the hardcoded version-pin assertion strings must be updated in lockstep when bumping the lockfile.~~ ✅ **already inline-closed in slice 020M fix-round-2** (commit `37bbf5e`). The REGENERATION INVARIANT callout added to ADOPT-001 §12.7.13 explicitly names the four hardcoded `assert yaml.__version__ ==` / `assert jsonschema.__version__ ==` sites that must be updated in lockstep. The TF entry filed by the R2 safety reviewer was redundant with the inline closure; pruned in slice 020N STATUS.md update.\\n\\n## Tracked-forward items from 020N (conflict-gate hash-pinning)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/codex-extras-fix-round-23-audit.log:22:This is the SAME class of issue closed for `tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` paths in WP-SCP-022 020Q (closes TF-006) — namely, files that conftest CAN parse syntactically (JSON) but should NOT be policy-evaluated because they exist for a different purpose. Review-archive JSON files are governance artifacts (Sonnet R1 lens output), not policy data.\n./docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/codex-extras-fix-round-23-audit.log:26:In `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh`, in the target-selection loop (around line 180-200 where `tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` is already excluded), add a case for `docs/reviews/*` paths. Pattern mirror:\n./docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/codex-extras-fix-round-23-audit.log:30:      tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*)\n./docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/codex-extras-fix-round-23-audit.log:36:      docs/reviews/*)\n./docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/codex-extras-fix-round-23-audit.log:38:          printf '::debug::skipping %s: governance review artifact (Claude SDK output / dispatch package), not policy input\\n' \"$target\"\n./docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/codex-extras-fix-round-23-audit.log:45:Why `docs/reviews/*` (broad) and not `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/*` (narrow):\n./docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/codex-extras-fix-round-23-audit.log:54:- **Fix-round-23** (2026-05-11): closed the CI blocker for `policy-check / scp/policy-check` (required check on main). `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh` target-selection loop now skips `docs/reviews/*` paths (consistent with the `tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` exclusion closed in WP-SCP-022 020Q). Review-archive JSON files are governance artifacts, not policy input data; their inclusion in the conftest scan was a long-standing bug that this slice's fix-round-17+ committed enough archive files to surface.\n./docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/codex-extras-fix-round-23-audit.log:62:- Look for any direct unit tests of `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh` in `tests/`; if any exist and they cover the target-selection loop, add a matching positive case for `docs/reviews/*` exclusion.\n./docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/codex-extras-fix-round-23-audit.log:75:- `bash -c 'grep -qE \"docs/reviews/\\*\\)|governance review artifact\" lib/policy_check_invocation.sh'`\n./docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/codex-extras-fix-round-23-audit.log:86:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' lib/policy_check_invocation.sh\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\nscp_policy_check_emit_error() {\\n  local code=\\\"$1\\\"\\n  local file=\\\"$2\\\"\\n  local message=\\\"$3\\\"\\n\\n  if [ \\\"${GITHUB_ACTIONS:-}\\\" = \\\"true\\\" ]; then\\n    printf '::error file=%s,title=%s::%s\\\\n' \\\"$file\\\" \\\"$code\\\" \\\"$message\\\"\\n    return\\n  fi\\n\\n  printf '%s %s: %s\\\\n' \\\"$code\\\" \\\"$file\\\" \\\"$message\\\" >&2\\n}\\n\\nscp_policy_check_output_dir() {\\n  printf '%s\\\\n' \\\"${SCP_POLICY_CHECK_OUTPUT_DIR:-output/findings}\\\"\\n}\\n\\nscp_policy_check_policy_dir() {\\n  local policy_root=\\\"${SCP_POLICY_CHECK_POLICY_ROOT:-policies}\\\"\\n  local rule_set=\\\"${SCP_RULE_SET:-starter}\\\"\\n  if [ \\\"$rule_set\\\" = \\\"starter\\\" ]; then\\n    printf '%s\\\\n' \\\"$policy_root\\\"\\n    return\\n  fi\\n  printf '%s/%s\\\\n' \\\"$policy_root\\\" \\\"$rule_set\\\"\\n}\\n\\nscp_policy_check_sha256_file() {\\n  local path=\\\"$1\\\"\\n\\n  if command -v shasum >/dev/null 2>&1; then\\n    shasum -a 256 \\\"$path\\\" | awk '{print $1}'\\n    return\\n  fi\\n\\n  sha256sum \\\"$path\\\" | awk '{print $1}'\\n}\\n\\nscp_policy_check_verify_runtime_binary() {\\n  local label=\\\"$1\\\"\\n  local path=\\\"$2\\\"\\n  local expected=\\\"$3\\\"\\n  local actual\\n\\n  if [ -z \\\"$path\\\" ] || [ -z \\\"$expected\\\" ]; then\\n    scp_policy_check_emit_error \\\"SCP-E001\\\" \\\"${path:-<unset>}\\\" \\\"${label} runtime binary verification refused: empty path or expected SHA256 (caller must set both)\\\"\\n    return 1\\n  fi\\n\\n  if [ ! -f \\\"$path\\\" ]; then\\n    scp_policy_check_emit_error \\\"SCP-E001\\\" \\\"$path\\\" \\\"${label} runtime binary is missing at the configured path\\\"\\n    return 1\\n  fi\\n\\n  actual=\\\"$(scp_policy_check_sha256_file \\\"$path\\\")\\\"\\n  if [ \\\"$actual\\\" != \\\"$expected\\\" ]; then\\n    scp_policy_check_emit_error \\\"SCP-E001\\\" \\\"$path\\\" \\\"${label} runtime binary failed SHA256 verification immediately before execution\\\"\\n    return 1\\n  fi\\n}\\n\\nscp_policy_check_verify_runtime_binaries() {\\n  local missing=()\\n  [ -z \\\"${SCP_POLICY_CHECK_OPA_BIN:-}\\\" ] && missing+=(\\\"SCP_POLICY_CHECK_OPA_BIN\\\")\\n  [ -z \\\"${SCP_POLICY_CHECK_OPA_SHA256:-}\\\" ] && missing+=(\\\"SCP_POLICY_CHECK_OPA_SHA256\\\")\\n  [ -z \\\"${SCP_POLICY_CHECK_CONFTEST_BIN:-}\\\" ] && missing+=(\\\"SCP_POLICY_CHECK_CONFTEST_BIN\\\")\\n  [ -z \\\"${SCP_POLICY_CHECK_CONFTEST_SHA256:-}\\\" ] && missing+=(\\\"SCP_POLICY_CHECK_CONFTEST_SHA256\\\")\\n  if [ ${#missing[@]} -gt 0 ]; then\\n    scp_policy_check_emit_error \\\"SCP-E001\\\" \\\"<env>\\\" \\\"runtime binary verification refused: required env vars unset: ${missing[*]}\\\"\\n    return 1\\n  fi\\n\\n  scp_policy_check_verify_runtime_binary \\\\\\n    \\\"OPA\\\" \\\\\\n    \\\"$SCP_POLICY_CHECK_OPA_BIN\\\" \\\\\\n    \\\"$SCP_POLICY_CHECK_OPA_SHA256\\\" || return 1\\n\\n  scp_policy_check_verify_runtime_binary \\\\\\n    \\\"Conftest\\\" \\\\\\n    \\\"$SCP_POLICY_CHECK_CONFTEST_BIN\\\" \\\\\\n    \\\"$SCP_POLICY_CHECK_CONFTEST_SHA256\\\" || return 1\\n}\\n\\nscp_policy_check_init_outputs() {\\n  local output_dir\\n  local policy_dir\\n  local rule_config_path\\n\\n  output_dir=\\\"$(scp_policy_check_output_dir)\\\"\\n  policy_dir=\\\"$(scp_policy_check_policy_dir)\\\"\\n  rule_config_path=\\\"${SCP_RULE_CONFIG_PATH:-.scp/rule-config.yaml}\\\"\\n\\n  if [ -e \\\"$rule_config_path\\\" ] && [ ! -f \\\"$rule_config_path\\\" ]; then\\n    scp_policy_check_emit_error \\\"SCP-E002\\\" \\\"$rule_config_path\\\" \\\"rule-config-path must point to a regular file when present\\\"\\n    return 1\\n  fi\\n\\n  if [ -e \\\"$policy_dir\\\" ] && [ ! -d \\\"$policy_dir\\\" ]; then\\n    scp_policy_check_emit_error \\\"SCP-E002\\\" \\\"$policy_dir\\\" \\\"policy bundle path must be a directory when present\\\"\\n    return 1\\n  fi\\n\\n  mkdir -p \\\"$output_dir\\\"\\n  printf '[]\\\\n' > \\\"${output_dir}/policy-findings.json\\\"\\n  printf '[]\\\\n' > \\\"${output_dir}/disabled-rules.json\\\"\\n  printf '[]\\\\n' > \\\"${output_dir}/waivers-applied.json\\\"\\n  printf '{\\\"run\\\": false, \\\"disagreements\\\": []}\\\\n' > \\\"${output_dir}/conflict-gate.json\\\"\\n}\\n\\nscp_policy_check_run() {\\n  local changed_files_path\\n  local conftest_json\\n  local data_dir\\n  local output_dir\\n  local policy_dir\\n  local rule_config_path\\n  local waivers_path\\n  local -a conftest_args\\n  # Closes WP-SCP-022 slice 020D1/020H.1 CI fixpoint #1 (2026-04-30):\\n  # `local -a targets` (without initialiser) declares the array but\\n  # leaves it unset. Under `set -u`, `${#targets[@]}` then trips\\n  # 'unbound variable' if the loop's case statement never runs the\\n  # `targets+=(\\\"$target\\\")` branch — which happens when every file in\\n  # the changed-files manifest has an extension conftest cannot parse\\n  # (.md, .py, .rego, .sh, ...). The 020D1 PR diff was workflow-yaml-\\n  # only so the bug was masked; 020H.1's diff is .md-only and\\n  # tripped it. Initialising to empty fixes the cold-start case.\\n  local -a targets=()\\n  local target\\n\\n  scp_policy_check_init_outputs || return 1\\n\\n  changed_files_path=\\\"${SCP_CHANGED_FILES_PATH:-changed-files.txt}\\\"\\n  output_dir=\\\"$(scp_policy_check_output_dir)\\\"\\n  policy_dir=\\\"$(scp_policy_check_policy_dir)\\\"\\n  rule_config_path=\\\"${SCP_RULE_CONFIG_PATH:-.scp/rule-config.yaml}\\\"\\n  waivers_path=\\\"${SCP_WAIVERS_PATH:-output/findings/waivers.json}\\\"\\n\\n  if [ ! -f \\\"$changed_files_path\\\" ]; then\\n    scp_policy_check_emit_error \\\"SCP-E002\\\" \\\"$changed_files_path\\\" \\\"changed-files manifest is required before invoking Conftest\\\"\\n    return 1\\n  fi\\n\\n  if [ ! -d \\\"$policy_dir\\\" ]; then\\n    if [ \\\"${SCP_RULE_SET:-starter}\\\" = \\\"starter\\\" ] && [ \\\"$policy_dir\\\" = \\\"policies\\\" ]; then\\n      return 0\\n    fi\\n\\n    scp_policy_check_emit_error \\\"SCP-E002\\\" \\\"$policy_dir\\\" \\\"policy bundle path does not exist for the selected rule-set\\\"\\n    return 1\\n  fi\\n\\n  if ! find \\\"$policy_dir\\\" -type f -name '*.rego' -print -quit | grep -q .; then\\n    return 0\\n  fi\\n\\n  # WP-SCP-022 020C.1 selftest exposed: conftest can't parse .md /\\n  # other-text files; passing them in the target list crashes the\\n  # whole evaluation with `unknown parser: md`. Filter to file\\n  # extensions conftest can natively load. Manifest files\\n  # (package.json, pyproject.toml, go.mod) are already rewritten\\n  # into yaml surrogates by the workflow's \\\"Prepare manifest\\n  # evaluation targets\\\" step, so they enter this loop as `.yaml`.\\n  #\\n  # WP-SCP-022 slice 020Q (closes TF-006): also skip\\n  # `tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/**` paths — those fixtures exist\\n  # to be audited BY the conflict-gate test framework\\n  # (`tests/conflict_gate/test_conflict_gate.py`), which loads sibling\\n  # `waivers.json` / `.scp/rule-config.yaml` and passes them to OPA via\\n  # `--data`. Auditing them here from the production policy-check\\n  # workflow would fire raw rule denies (e.g. SCP-R-001 on a fixture\\n  # `services.yml` with an unapproved mode) without the suppression\\n  # context the fixture is designed to exercise. The fixture-corpus\\n  # invariant is enforced by the conflict-gate pytest layer; the\\n  # production policy-check should not re-audit these files.\\n  local target_basename\\n  local target_ext\\n  while IFS= read -r target; do\\n    if [ -z \\\"$target\\\" ]; then\\n      continue\\n    fi\\n    case \\\"$target\\\" in\\n      tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*)\\n        if [ \\\"${GITHUB_ACTIONS:-}\\\" = \\\"true\\\" ]; then\\n          printf '::debug::skipping %s: conflict-gate fixture (audited by pytest layer, closes 020Q)\\\\n' \\\"$target\\\"\\n        fi\\n        continue\\n        ;;\\n    esac\\n    target_basename=\\\"$(basename \\\"$target\\\")\\\"\\n    target_ext=\\\"${target_basename##*.}\\\"\\n    case \\\"$target_ext\\\" in\\n      yml|yaml|json|toml|hcl|ini|properties|cue|edn|xml)\\n        targets+=(\\\"$target\\\")\\n        ;;\\n      *)\\n        # Conftest cannot parse this file type; skip silently.\\n        # Document via debug for diagnosability.\\n        if [ \\\"${GITHUB_ACTIONS:-}\\\" = \\\"true\\\" ]; then\\n          printf '::debug::skipping %s: conftest has no parser for .%s\\\\n' \\\"$target\\\" \\\"$target_ext\\\"\\n        fi\\n        ;;\\n    esac\\n  done < \\\"$changed_files_path\\\"\\n\\n  if [ \\\"${#targets[@]}\\\" -eq 0 ]; then\\n    return 0\\n  fi\\n\\n  scp_policy_check_verify_runtime_binaries || return 1\\n\\n  if ! command -v conftest >/dev/null 2>&1; then\\n    scp_policy_check_emit_error \\\"SCP-E001\\\" \\\"conftest\\\" \\\"Conftest must be on PATH before invoking the shared policy-check library\\\"\\n    return 1\\n  fi\\n\\n  conftest_json=\\\"$(mktemp \\\"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/scp-conftest.XXXXXX.json\\\")\\\"\\n  conftest_args=(test --no-fail --output json --policy \\\"$policy_dir\\\")\\n\\n  # WP-SCP-022 slice 020C.1: wrap caller-side waivers + rule-config so\\n  # they land at predictable namespaces in the Rego data document\\n  # (data.waivers / data.rule_config) regardless of conftest's\\n  # filename-derived merge semantics. See policies/scp_common.rego.\\n  data_dir=\\\"$(mktemp -d \\\"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/scp-data.XXXXXX\\\")\\\"\\n\\n  if [ -f \\\"$waivers_path\\\" ]; then\\n    if ! python3 - \\\"$waivers_path\\\" \\\"${data_dir}/waivers.json\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport json\\nimport sys\\n\\nsource = sys.argv[1]\\ndest = sys.argv[2]\\ntry:\\n    with open(source, \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as handle:\\n        content = json.load(handle)\\nexcept Exception:\\n    # Defensive: malformed waivers.json should not crash the policy run;\\n    # SCP-R-002 will deny it as part of the regular evaluation.\\n    content = []\\nwith open(dest, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as handle:\\n    json.dump({\\\"waivers\\\": content}, handle)\\nPY\\n    then\\n      rm -rf \\\"$data_dir\\\"\\n      rm -f \\\"$conftest_json\\\"\\n      scp_policy_check_emit_error \\\"SCP-E002\\\" \\\"$waivers_path\\\" \\\"waivers data wrapper failed to write\\\"\\n      return 1\\n    fi\\n    conftest_args+=(--data \\\"${data_dir}/waivers.json\\\")\\n  fi\\n\\n  if [ -f \\\"$rule_config_path\\\" ]; then\\n    if ! python3 - \\\"$rule_config_path\\\" \\\"${data_dir}/rule_config.json\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport json\\nimport sys\\n\\ntry:\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/codex-extras-fix-round-1-audit.log:168:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n --no-heading -e '.*' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-correctness.json docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-safety_bypass.json docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-completeness_governance.json docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md scripts/enable-required-check.sh tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh .github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md docs/DECISIONS.md STATUS.md policies/VERSIONING.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-completeness_governance.json:1:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"result\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"success\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false,\\\"api_error_status\\\":null,\\\"duration_ms\\\":529727,\\\"duration_api_ms\\\":530585,\\\"num_turns\\\":23,\\\"result\\\":\\\"Now I have sufficient evidence to compile the structured review. Producing the findings report:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"review_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"r1-completeness_governance\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"slice\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"WP-SCP-024 024B-extras\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"lens\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"completeness_governance\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"verdict\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"NEEDS_FIXES\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"024B-extras maps all carry-forward findings to concrete artefacts: R8-CORR-001/003 closed upstream; R8-CORR-002 addressed (prior-entry detection correctly gated inside RESTORE_MODE=0 path); R8-SAFE-001 addressed via WARNING+CAUTION callouts in §12.8 and log block; R8-SAFE-002 addressed via working-tree diff check; bootstrap defect addressed via paths-ignore (though this is dead code — see MIN-001). Step-7 operator-interactive demo is correctly unchecked at R1, placeholder file exists, and DISPATCH-NOTE AC is merge-blocking. Plan-doc §6 notes 024C gated on both halves + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 (correct). D-047 is filed, dated 2026-05-10, cites the split, and covers all extras deliverables. Four MAJ findings block fixpoint: VERSIONING.md omits the four new flags from the breaking-change surface list; the forward-mode safety check applies a jq head_branch filter that achieves the same exclusion as the forbidden &branch= API filter, defeating the check for canonical PR-only adopters; three --restore incompatibility test cases are absent; and the MERGE-BLOCKING step-7 demo lacks a formal TF entry in STATUS.md tracked-forward items. Three MIN findings: paths+paths-ignore conflict (dead code); D-047 rationale omits the escape hatch flag name; §12.8 Gate 3 overstates --expected-wrapper-sha as REQUIRED. No descope recommended.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"findings\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CG-R1-MAJ-001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MAJ\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"VERSIONING.md §Branch-protection helper breaking-change surface list does not enumerate the four new flags introduced by 024B-extras.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"policies/VERSIONING.md §Branch-protection helper lists --repo, --branch, --plan, --no-enforce-admins, --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate only. Four new flags absent: --expected-wrapper-sha, --i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement, --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks, --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification. Grep for any of these four in VERSIONING.md returns no matches.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Removing any of these flags post-024B is a MAJOR-breaking change per VERSIONING.md semver contract, but without enumeration operators and adopters have no documented guarantee. The contract is ambiguous on whether these flags are protected.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add all four new flags to the Branch-protection helper bullet in VERSIONING.md §'What counts as a breaking change', mirroring the existing --no-enforce-admins / --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate entries.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CG-R1-MAJ-002\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MAJ\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Forward-mode safety check queries without &branch= (correct per spec) but then applies jq `select(.head_branch == $default_branch)`, which achieves the same exclusion as the forbidden API branch filter and defeats the check for canonical PR-only adopters.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"enable-required-check.sh:465: `map(select(.head_branch == $default_branch)) | length`. DISPATCH-NOTE spec: 'query WITHOUT &branch= filter (PR-triggered runs have head-branch = feature branch; branch filter defeats gate).' Canonical wrapper templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl triggers only on pull_request:; all its runs have head_branch = feature branch, never matching $default_branch. run_count is always 0 for canonical adopters.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Safety check perpetually returns exit 2 for any adopter using the canonical PR-only wrapper, forcing all operators to use --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci even for established adopters. The check is non-functional for its primary use case.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Remove the jq `select(.head_branch == $default_branch)` filter; use `.workflow_runs | length` to count all successful runs regardless of triggering branch. Update test fixtures to use head_branch values from PR-triggered runs to cover the corrected logic.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CG-R1-MAJ-003\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MAJ\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Three --restore incompatibility test cases specified in the DISPATCH-NOTE are absent from test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE §scope restore tests: '--restore + forward-mode-flag incompatibility (--no-enforce-admins, --plan, --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate, --expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci).' Grep for 'incompatib|cannot be combined|restore.*plan|restore.*no-enforce' in the test file yields one match only: line 2108 (--expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci forward-mode mutex). --restore+--plan, --restore+--no-enforce-admins, --restore+--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate: absent.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Three incompatibility guards at enable-required-check.sh:224-239 are untested. A regression silently allowing --restore with forward-mode flags would not be caught by CI.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add three run_restore_case invocations: (1) with --plan flag → exit 2, stderr containing 'cannot be combined with --plan'; (2) with --no-enforce-admins → exit 2, stderr 'cannot be combined with --no-enforce-admins'; (3) with --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate → exit 2, matching stderr.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CG-R1-MAJ-004\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MAJ\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MERGE-BLOCKING step-7 operator-interactive demo has no formal TF tracking entry in STATUS.md tracked-forward items section.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"STATUS.md 'Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-024 024B-core / 024B-extras' lists FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001, FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001, TF-024B-SCAFFOLDER-023E002-UPDATE. No TF-024B-002 or equivalent entry for step-7 demo. Only the narrative Today's chain bullet #4 references the placeholder. DISPATCH-NOTE instructs R1 to 'verify cross-reference to TF-024B-002 or equivalent tracking entry.'\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The MERGE-BLOCKING gate is not machine-surfaced. A future session resuming from STATUS.md alone would not detect the open gate. Governance continuity invariant violated: the open merge-blocking item is invisible to the TF-tracking mechanism.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add a named TF entry (e.g., TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001) to STATUS.md tracked-forward items for 024B-core/extras with status (open), description referencing the placeholder path, and the merge-blocking condition.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CG-R1-MIN-001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MIN\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CI workflow uses both paths: and paths-ignore: for the same pull_request event; GitHub Actions silently ignores paths-ignore when paths is also present, making paths-ignore dead code.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\".github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml lines 18-21 combine paths: [...024[C-Z]*/**...STATUS.md] with paths-ignore: ['docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**']. GitHub Actions docs: 'paths-ignore is ignored when paths is also present.' The paths filter already excludes 024[AB]* by only matching 024[C-Z]*, so behavior is correct but paths-ignore is a no-op.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Functional behavior is correct. If paths is narrowed in a future edit, paths-ignore would remain silently inert, creating a latent correctness risk. Confusing to code reviewers who expect paths-ignore to do something.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Remove the paths-ignore line; add an inline comment on the paths filter explaining that 024[C-Z]* glob pattern implicitly excludes 024A/024B tooling slices, which was the intent of paths-ignore.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CG-R1-MIN-002\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MIN\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"D-047 rationale does not name --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification or describe its trust-model consequence; R8-SAFE-001 mitigation plan requires D-047 to acknowledge the escape hatch explicitly.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"docs/DECISIONS.md D-047 rationale mentions 'bootstrap guard' and 'release artifact' but does not contain '--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification'. DISPATCH-NOTE R8-SAFE-001 mitigation: 'D-047 rationale acknowledging escape hatch.' The trust-model claim ('Gate 2 wrapper-SHA pin is explicit operator consent becomes inaccurate when bypassed') is absent.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Decision record is an incomplete audit of the R8-SAFE-001 governance action. An operator reading D-047 alone cannot determine the trust-model risk of the bypass flag or that its use was knowingly accepted at dispatch.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Amend D-047 rationale to name --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification, note it bypasses Gate 2 SHA-pin verification, and confirm that bypass is auditable via the log block CAUTION line per §12.8.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CG-R1-MIN-003\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MIN\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 describes --expected-wrapper-sha as REQUIRED but the script does not enforce its presence in forward mode.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3: '--expected-wrapper-sha REQUIRED — not optional/advisory.' enable-required-check.sh check_forward_mode_safety():472: `if [ -n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$EXPECTED_WRAPPER_SHA\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" ]` — validation is conditional on the flag being supplied; the script does not exit non-zero when it is absent. An operator can re-enable in forward mode without --expected-wrapper-sha.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Documentation overstates the script's enforcement level. An operator relying on the REQUIRED label as a technical guard receives no script-level rejection if the flag is omitted during a break-glass Gate 3 re-enable.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Either (a) add script enforcement that requires --expected-wrapper-sha when prior restore evidence is detected (auto-detect Gate 3 context), or (b) amend §12.8 Gate 3 to say 'strongly recommended; the script validates the SHA when provided but does not mandate it' and remove the REQUIRED label.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CG-R1-nit-001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"nit\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"STATUS.md Today's chain entry for 024B-extras omits a note that the extras-parking branch can be deleted after both halves merge.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"STATUS.md 'Today's chain (2026-05-10)' has 4 bullets; none mentions feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking branch cleanup. DISPATCH-NOTE intro states: 'The parking branch can be deleted once both halves merge.'\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Minor housekeeping gap; the parking branch remains open indefinitely. No governance invariant broken.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add a 5th bullet: 'feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking can be deleted once 024B-core + 024B-extras both merge (audit trail intact in git history + r8-archive preserved).'\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CG-R1-nit-002\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"nit\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE specifies an absolute path normalisation test for --restore mode; no such test is present in the test file.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE §scope restore tests: 'absolute path normalisation.' All run_restore_case invocations in test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh use relative path 'pre-state.json'; no case passes an absolute path argument.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Minor coverage fidelity gap vs. DISPATCH-NOTE spec. No functional defect expected (bash/python handle relative and absolute paths uniformly for cat/open).\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add one restore test case passing an absolute path via `$(pwd)/pre-state.json` and asserting exit 0 to satisfy the DISPATCH-NOTE spec literally.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CG-R1-nit-003\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"nit\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Step-7 placeholder file lacks an evidence template; the operator must cross-reference the DISPATCH-NOTE to know what to commit.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md contains only: 'This file is reserved for the operator-interactive step-7 restore round-trip evidence.' No template for: test repo name, before-state JSON, restore-mode invocation log, after-state JSON, byte-for-byte match assertion result.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Minor operator-ergonomics gap; no governance invariant broken. The DISPATCH-NOTE is co-located and describes the required evidence, but the operator must look in two places.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Expand the placeholder with section headers matching the required evidence format: test-repo, pre-state-capture, restore-invocation-command, after-state-GET, match-assertion-result, operator-timestamp.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\\n```\\\",\\\"stop_reason\\\":\\\"end_turn\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"63ff13ee-81f1-4f0b-918f-ac552c57e154\\\",\\\"total_cost_usd\\\":1.1542960500000001,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":13,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":118115,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":892626,\\\"output_tokens\\\":29439,\\\"server_tool_use\\\":{\\\"web_search_requests\\\":0,\\\"web_fetch_requests\\\":0},\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":118115,\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0},\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"iterations\\\":[{\\\"input_tokens\\\":1,\\\"output_tokens\\\":16618,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":122151,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":3345,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":3345},\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\"}],\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"modelUsage\\\":{\\\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":1823,\\\"outputTokens\\\":26,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":0,\\\"cacheCreationInputTokens\\\":0,\\\"webSearchRequests\\\":0,\\\"costUSD\\\":0.0019529999999999999,\\\"contextWindow\\\":200000,\\\"maxOutputTokens\\\":32000},\\\"claude-sonnet-4-6\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":13,\\\"outputTokens\\\":29439,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":892626,\\\"cacheCreationInputTokens\\\":118115,\\\"webSearchRequests\\\":0,\\\"costUSD\\\":1.1523430499999998,\\\"contextWindow\\\":200000,\\\"maxOutputTokens\\\":32000}},\\\"permission_denials\\\":[],\\\"terminal_reason\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"fast_mode_state\\\":\\\"off\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"af8b816c-15e1-4921-9f84-500815c4c806\\\"}\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-correctness.json:1:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"result\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"success\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false,\\\"api_error_status\\\":null,\\\"duration_ms\\\":655432,\\\"duration_api_ms\\\":656075,\\\"num_turns\\\":18,\\\"result\\\":\\\"I now have all the information needed to produce the correctness review. Let me compile the findings.\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"reviewer_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"R1-correctness\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"lens\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"correctness\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"slice\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"WP-SCP-024 024B-extras\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"verdict\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"FAIL\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Seven findings: 1 CRIT, 3 MAJ, 3 MIN. CRIT: the paths-ignore bootstrap guard is incomplete — the 024B-extras PR changes STATUS.md, which matches the workflow paths filter and is NOT excluded by paths-ignore (which only covers 024[AB]*/**). The workflow fires, resolves the 024B-extras DISPATCH-NOTE (cascade-status: not applicable), and exits 2 because --allow-not-applicable is absent from the workflow invocation. This is the exact self-blocking defect R7 claimed to address, persisting because STATUS.md was not considered. Three MAJ defects follow: (1) check_forward_mode_safety applies a client-side jq head_branch == default_branch filter that achieves the same exclusion as the &branch= parameter the dispatch note explicitly prohibited — PR-triggered runs are silently dropped, causing false rejections for cold-start adopters; (2) ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 states '--expected-wrapper-sha is REQUIRED when prior restore evidence exists; omitting it rejects with exit 2' but the guard is gated on the flag being present — the Gate 3 requirement is silently bypassable; (3) three restore+forward-mode mutex test cases are absent (--restore+--plan, --restore+--no-enforce-admins, --restore+--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate). All other major areas check out: GET→PUT transform correct, APPLY_FAIL pattern correct, required_signatures POST/DELETE correct, prior-entry detection guard correct (R8-CORR-002 closed), cascade-status regex clean (R8-CORR-001 closed), --expected-wrapper-sha tag validation correct, ADOPT-001 §12.8 three-gate structure correct.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"findings\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CORR-001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CRIT\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Bootstrap defect persists: workflow self-blocks 024B-extras PR via STATUS.md trigger path.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.yml paths filter includes 'STATUS.md'; paths-ignore is 'docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**'. DISPATCH-NOTE scope lists STATUS.md as an explicit deliverable (aa5be78 commit message confirms). When the PR changes STATUS.md, GitHub evaluates the trigger as: STATUS.md matches paths AND does NOT match paths-ignore → workflow fires. The 'Resolve dispatch note path' step then runs git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD -- 'docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024*/DISPATCH-NOTE.md' | head -n1, which finds docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md (also changed). DISPATCH-NOTE line 9 declares cascade-status: not applicable. The 'Check invocation log entry' step invokes check-invocation-log-entry.sh without --allow-not-applicable, so the script exits 2 with 'ERROR: cascade-status: not applicable found, but --allow-not-applicable was not passed.' CI fails.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"024B-extras cannot achieve the CI-green acceptance criterion through its own gate. The introducing PR self-blocks — the same class as R7 bootstrap defect, now via the STATUS.md path rather than the DISPATCH-NOTE path.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Either (a) in the 'Check invocation log entry' step, detect cascade-status: not applicable in the resolved dispatch note and exit 0 (tooling-slice short-circuit), or (b) restrict the dispatch note glob in the resolution step to '024[C-Z]*/DISPATCH-NOTE.md' so tooling DISPATCH-NOTEs are never found, and exit 0 when the glob returns empty. Option (b) is narrower and avoids adding --allow-not-applicable to the workflow (which would permit cohort slices to bypass by embedding a tooling DISPATCH-NOTE).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CORR-002\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MAJ\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"check_forward_mode_safety client-side jq filter reinstates the excluded &branch= parameter, silently dropping PR-triggered runs from the safety check count.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Line 464: gh api '...runs?workflow_id=${workflow_id}&status=success&created>=${created_since}' — correct, no &branch=. Line 465: jq '.workflow_runs | map(select(.head_branch == $default_branch)) | length'. For a PR-triggered run, head_branch is the source branch (e.g. feature/pim-adopt), not main. select(.head_branch == $default_branch) excludes all such runs. This is arithmetically equivalent to ?&branch=main. DISPATCH-NOTE explicitly states: 'NO &branch= filter on workflow-runs API (PR-triggered runs have head-branch = feature branch, not default; branch filter defeats gate).' The implementation defeats the gate via the client-side path. Fake-gh fixtures all use head_branch:'main', so the test suite does not expose this.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Forward-mode invocation against a newly onboarded adopter whose only recent successful runs are PR-triggered (typical cold-start) fails with 'no successful workflow runs found' even though the wrapper is demonstrably functional. The --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci bypass is needed every time, defeating the gate's safety purpose.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Remove the select(.head_branch == ...) jq filter entirely: run_count=$(... | jq '.workflow_runs | length'). The window is already bounded by ?status=success&created>=${created_since}, so counting all successful runs regardless of head_branch satisfies the DISPATCH-NOTE spec. Add a test fixture with head_branch:'feature/pim-adopt' to expose the bug in regression.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CORR-003\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MAJ\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Gate 3 enforcement gap: --expected-wrapper-sha is not required when prior restore evidence exists, contradicting ADOPT-001 §12.8's stated contract.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3: 'If the flag is omitted, re-enable is rejected with exit 2.' Implementation (lines 472-483): the prior_restore_evidence_present() check only executes inside if [ -n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$EXPECTED_WRAPPER_SHA\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" ]. If the operator runs forward-mode without --expected-wrapper-sha after completing Gate 1, the outer guard short-circuits to noop — no error, no exit 2. Gate 3 is thus advisory (documentation-enforced only) rather than code-enforced. No test case exercises the path where restore evidence IS present and --expected-wrapper-sha IS absent.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"An operator who completes Gate 1 (restore) and then mistakenly re-enables via plain forward-mode (without --expected-wrapper-sha) bypasses Gate 3 entirely. The re-enable may run against a wrapper still pinned to the defective SCP SHA, re-arming the broken gate. The audit log does not record a Gate-3 bypass because no mechanism fires.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Before the existing --expected-wrapper-sha guard, unconditionally check prior_restore_evidence_present. If evidence is found AND --expected-wrapper-sha is absent, emit an error and exit 2. This enforces the contract stated in ADOPT-001 §12.8 in code rather than only in documentation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CORR-004\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MAJ\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Three --restore + forward-mode flag mutex test cases are absent from the test suite despite being explicitly required by the DISPATCH-NOTE acceptance criteria.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE AC: 'Tests: --restore + forward-mode-flag incompatibility (--no-enforce-admins, --plan, --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate, --expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci).' The enable-sha-mutex test (line 2078) covers the --expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci pair. No test case invokes run_restore_case with --plan (guards at line 224), --no-enforce-admins (guard at line 228), or --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate (guard at line 232). The implementation logic for these guards is present and appears correct, but the guards have no test coverage.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A regression removing any of the three guards would not be caught by the test suite. The guards are the only enforcement against operators accidentally combining restore-mode with contradictory forward-mode flags.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add three run_restore_case test cases: (a) --plan → expected exit 2, stderr contains 'cannot be combined with --plan'; (b) --no-enforce-admins → expected exit 2, stderr contains 'cannot be combined with --no-enforce-admins'; (c) --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate → expected exit 2, stderr contains 'cannot be combined with --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate'.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CORR-005\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MIN\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"D-047 rationale omits explicit naming of the --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification escape hatch flag, violating R8-SAFE-001 mitigation requirement.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"R8-SAFE-001 mitigation (DISPATCH-NOTE §Carry-forward): 'WARNING + CAUTION callouts in ADOPT-001 §12.8 + log-block CAUTION line + D-047 rationale acknowledging escape hatch.' DECISIONS.md D-047 row (line 93) names ADOPT-001 §12.8, restore mode, and CI wiring but never names the --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification flag by string in the decision rationale. ADOPT-001 §12.8 WARNING/CAUTION callouts are present and correct; the code emits the CAUTION log line (line 475-476); but D-047 itself is the governance anchor for the escape hatch and should document it explicitly.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Future review of D-047 will not surface the escape hatch's existence or its trust-model implications without cross-referencing ADOPT-001 §12.8 separately. The R8-SAFE-001 closure is technically incomplete at the decision-record level.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add one sentence to D-047 rationale naming --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification as the emergency Gate-2 bypass and stating that its use is logged in the audit trail per R8-SAFE-001.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CORR-006\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MIN\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags fetches only 100 tags without Link-header pagination, silently missing tags beyond the first 100.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Line 423: gh api 'repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/git/refs/tags?per_page=100'. GitHub paginates at per_page=100; if >100 tags exist, subsequent pages are never fetched. The jq pipeline on line 431 processes only the single-page response. The SCP repo currently has far fewer than 100 release tags, so this does not fail today.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Once the SCP repo accumulates more than 100 release tags, validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags may report 'SHA not found in release-tag cache' for valid tags beyond page 1, blocking Gate 3 re-enable with a false negative.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Replace the single API call with a paginated loop using the gh --paginate flag or --header 'Link' parsing, or limit validation to recent tags only (e.g. refs starting with 'v' sorted by creation date, last 100). Nit-level urgency today but worth filing as a tracked-forward item before the estate reaches 100 releases.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CORR-007\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MIN\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No test exercises the working-tree-only restore evidence path in prior_restore_evidence_present (R8-SAFE-002 mitigation).\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"R8-SAFE-002 mitigation: 'also check working-tree diff via git diff HEAD branch-protection-log.md.' The enable-expected-sha test (line 1945) has restore evidence in both HEAD (committed at line 2007) AND the working tree (appended via printf at lines 2008-2022). There is no test where restore evidence is ONLY in the working tree (not yet committed). The git diff HEAD path in prior_restore_evidence_present (line 409) would catch this case in production, but it is never the sole path exercised by any test.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A regression that breaks the working-tree diff component of prior_restore_evidence_present (e.g. a path quoting bug) would not be caught. The committed-log path would still pass all existing tests.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add a test case for enable-expected-sha-wt-only: commit the log WITHOUT restore evidence, then append restore evidence to the working tree (printf >> log), run run_enable_case with --expected-wrapper-sha <valid-sha>, expect exit 0. This isolates the git diff HEAD path.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\\n```\\\",\\\"stop_reason\\\":\\\"end_turn\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"0eb1f737-21a1-4304-994a-ff982e77e5ad\\\",\\\"total_cost_usd\\\":1.4023415999999997,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":11,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":148740,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":842552,\\\"output_tokens\\\":39326,\\\"server_tool_use\\\":{\\\"web_search_requests\\\":0,\\\"web_fetch_requests\\\":0},\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":148740,\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0},\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"iterations\\\":[{\\\"input_tokens\\\":1,\\\"output_tokens\\\":21645,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":154213,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":1908,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":1908},\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\"}],\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"modelUsage\\\":{\\\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":1753,\\\"outputTokens\\\":25,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":0,\\\"cacheCreationInputTokens\\\":0,\\\"webSearchRequests\\\":0,\\\"costUSD\\\":0.001878,\\\"contextWindow\\\":200000,\\\"maxOutputTokens\\\":32000},\\\"claude-sonnet-4-6\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":11,\\\"outputTokens\\\":39326,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":842552,\\\"cacheCreationInputTokens\\\":148740,\\\"webSearchRequests\\\":0,\\\"costUSD\\\":1.4004636000000001,\\\"contextWindow\\\":200000,\\\"maxOutputTokens\\\":32000}},\\\"permission_denials\\\":[],\\\"terminal_reason\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"fast_mode_state\\\":\\\"off\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"487e026e-dd7e-449b-ac98-0aadfdf1e36e\\\"}\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-safety_bypass.json:1:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"result\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"success\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false,\\\"api_error_status\\\":null,\\\"duration_ms\\\":725242,\\\"duration_api_ms\\\":725718,\\\"num_turns\\\":17,\\\"result\\\":\\\"I now have enough information to produce the structured findings report.\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"review_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"R1-SAFETY_BYPASS-024B-EXTRAS-2026-05-10\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"slice\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"WP-SCP-024 024B-extras\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"lens\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SAFETY_BYPASS\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"verdict\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"NOT_FIXPOINT\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Four MAJ and four MIN/nit findings; no CRIT. Every defect produces some observable signal, but two MAJ findings allow API mutations to succeed despite guards being circumvented. SAFE-MAJ-001: Forward-mode jq post-filter (head_branch == default_branch) is functionally identical to the prohibited API ?branch= filter. The canonical wrapper (pull_request trigger only, confirmed via templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl) never produces head_branch=main runs; the safety gate is permanently useless for normal adopters, training routine bypass-flag usage. SAFE-MAJ-002: restore pre-state JSON with enforce_admins: {enabled: 0} bypasses the ACK guard (jq // treats integer 0 as non-null/non-false; bash '0' != 'false') while Python bool(0)=False silently applies enforce_admins=false via PUT; verification failure fires after the mutation. SAFE-MAJ-003: prior_restore_evidence_present's second return-0 block (grep 'Restoring TO:') is target-agnostic; a Gate-1 entry for adopter A satisfies Gate-3's Gate-1 prerequisite for any other target, collapsing per-adopter gate integrity. SAFE-MAJ-004: CI bootstrap defect incompletely closed: paths-ignore covers 024[AB]*/** but STATUS.md is an unconditional paths trigger; a tooling slice modifying STATUS.md triggers the workflow against the tooling DISPATCH-NOTE (cascade-status: not applicable), FAIL-CLOSED exit 2 blocks the introducing PR. SAFE-MIN-001: no ACK for required_pull_request_reviews=null on restore. SAFE-MIN-002: tag validation capped at per_page=100, causing false-negative for repos with >100 release tags. SAFE-MIN-003: forward-mode required_signatures POST lacks the 404-suppression present in restore mode. SAFE-NIT-001: hardcoded SCP repo name in tag validation.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"findings\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SAFE-MAJ-001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MAJ\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Forward-mode jq post-filter select(.head_branch == $default_branch) is functionally identical to the ?branch= API filter the DISPATCH-NOTE explicitly prohibits, making the prior-green-CI safety gate permanently useless for PR-only wrapper adopters.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"enable-required-check.sh:465 applies jq 'map(select(.head_branch == $default_branch))' after the API call. Canonical wrapper (templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl:5-7) only has pull_request trigger; PR-triggered runs have head_branch = source branch, never default branch. run_count is always 0 for normal adopters. Fake_gh guard (test:262-265) correctly rejects ?branch= in API endpoint but does not catch the equivalent jq post-filter exclusion.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Every adopter with a PR-only wrapper appears as 'no prior green CI'; operators must routinely pass --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci as the default, defeating the gate entirely. D-047 claim that forward-mode safety check uses 'no branch filter' is misleading; the post-filter achieves identical exclusion of PR-triggered runs.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Remove the jq head_branch filter or replace with '.workflow_runs | length' (count all successful runs without branch filtering). The existing fake_gh API guard is correct and sufficient for the no-API-branch-filter requirement.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SAFE-MAJ-002\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MAJ\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"restore pre-state JSON with enforce_admins: {enabled: 0} (integer zero) bypasses the posture-degradation ACK guard while Python bool(0)=False causes the PUT to apply enforce_admins=false without --i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"enable-required-check.sh:624: jq '.enforce_admins.enabled // false' with integer 0 returns '0' (jq // only substitutes for null/boolean-false; 0 is neither). Bash '0' == 'false' is false → ACK not required. Python transform line 358: bool(0)=False → PUT body has enforce_admins: false. Verification then compares 'false' vs '0', sets FAIL=1 and exits 1, but the API state is already mutated.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"An operator crafting or receiving a pre-state JSON with enabled: 0 instead of false disables admin enforcement without the required ACK. Script exits 1 (verification failure) but branch protection is already degraded. D-047 trust-model claim of posture-degradation completeness is inaccurate pending this fix.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Use RESTORE_PAYLOAD (transformed, already bool-coerced) for degradation checks instead of raw RESTORE_TARGET_JSON. Or extend bash check: jq '(.enforce_admins.enabled // false) | not' to correctly handle integers, nulls, and booleans uniformly.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SAFE-MAJ-003\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MAJ\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"prior_restore_evidence_present's second return-0 condition (grep 'Restoring TO:') is target-agnostic; a Gate-1 log entry for any adopter satisfies the Gate-3 Gate-1 prerequisite for any other target repo.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"enable-required-check.sh:413-417 — second if-block: 'printf committed+diff | grep -Fq \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Restoring TO:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"' with no $target guard. If branch-protection-log.md contains any prior restore entry ('Restoring TO:') for adopter A, running Gate 3 for adopter B passes the prerequisite check without a B-specific Gate 1. Test (line 1945) only exercises same-target path; no cross-target negative test exists.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Operator who completed Gate 1 for adopter A can execute Gate 3 for adopter B without a Gate-1 for B, bypassing sequential 3-gate playbook integrity. Manually committing a line containing 'Restoring TO:' also fakes Gate-1 evidence for all future targets.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Require both target string and 'Restoring TO:' to co-occur in the same log entry. Replace the second return-0 block with a compound check that requires both $target AND 'Restoring TO:' in close proximity, or merge the two conditions into one.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SAFE-MAJ-004\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MAJ\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CI bootstrap defect incompletely fixed: paths-ignore 024[AB]*/** excludes tooling DISPATCH-NOTE paths but STATUS.md is an unconditional paths trigger, so a tooling slice modifying STATUS.md triggers the workflow against the tooling DISPATCH-NOTE and FAIL-CLOSED blocks the introducing PR.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\".github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:17-21 — paths includes 'STATUS.md' with no corresponding paths-ignore entry. STATUS.md update is a listed 024B-extras deliverable. When triggered, the dispatch-note resolution step finds the 024B-extras DISPATCH-NOTE (cascade-status: not applicable); check-invocation-log-entry.sh exits 2 without --allow-not-applicable.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The 024B-extras PR is blocked by the workflow it introduces whenever STATUS.md is committed. D-047 trust-model claim of 'bootstrap path-filter closes introducing slice bootstrap defect' is inaccurate. Same issue applies to any future tooling slice (024G) modifying STATUS.md or branch-protection-log.md.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add STATUS.md and docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md to paths-ignore for 024[AB] slices, OR add an early-exit in the workflow when the resolved DISPATCH-NOTE has slice-type: tooling, OR pass --allow-not-applicable --tooling-slice-id derived from the DISPATCH-NOTE path.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SAFE-MIN-001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MIN\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No posture-degradation ACK is required when restore pre-state has required_pull_request_reviews: null, potentially silently removing PR review requirements added by the adopter after the initial enable-required-check.sh invocation.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"enable-required-check.sh:624-633 — posture-degradation guards cover only enforce_admins.enabled=false and empty required_status_checks.contexts. required_pull_request_reviews: null in before-JSON passes the type check (line 339, dict|None allowed) and is included verbatim in the PUT body without any ACK flag.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hardening gap: an adopter who added PR review requirements post-onboarding loses them silently during a break-glass restore. DISPATCH-NOTE acceptance criteria only names two ACK flags; this is within spec but represents an uncovered posture-degradation path.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Compare RESTORE_TARGET_JSON.required_pull_request_reviews vs BEFORE_JSON.required_pull_request_reviews at restore time; if target is null and current state is non-null, emit a WARNING and optionally require a third ACK flag.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SAFE-MIN-002\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MIN\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags fetches only the first 100 tags (per_page=100); valid release-tag SHAs beyond page 1 report as 'not found in release-tag SHA cache', false-blocking Gate 3.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"enable-required-check.sh:423 — 'gh api repos/.../git/refs/tags?per_page=100' with no pagination loop. If the SCP repo accumulates >100 release tags, a valid SHA on a later page causes exit 2 on --expected-wrapper-sha, forcing --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"False-negative gate failure (stricter, not weaker). Operator cannot use Gate 3 for a valid tag without the emergency escape hatch, undermining the rollback SLO. Becomes practically relevant as the tag count grows past 100.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add pagination loop (follow Link header) or document the 100-tag ceiling as a hard constraint in usage text. Alternatively, limit the search to the N most-recent tags with a documented cutoff.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SAFE-MIN-003\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MIN\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Forward-mode required_signatures POST is missing the 404-suppression handling present in restore mode, causing spurious APPLY_FAIL=1 and exit 1 when signatures are already enabled on the target repo.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"enable-required-check.sh:687 — forward mode: 'gh api -X POST .../required_signatures >/dev/null || APPLY_FAIL=1' with no 404 handling. Restore mode (lines 647-656) captures stderr and suppresses 404 with 'already in desired state' log. Test restore-post-404 (line 1896) covers restore path; no equivalent forward-mode test exists.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"An adopter with required_signatures pre-enabled sees APPLY_FAIL=1 and exit 1 despite branch protection being correctly set. Creates a confusing false-failure; operator may incorrectly conclude the apply failed and retry, polluting the audit log.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Apply the same 404-suppression pattern as restore mode: capture gh POST stderr to a temp file, grep for '404', suppress with log message. Reuse the pattern from lines 647-656 verbatim.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SAFE-NIT-001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"nit\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags hardcodes 'jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-' as the SCP repo path; breaks if the SCP repo is forked, renamed, or operated under a different owner.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"enable-required-check.sh:423,426 — literal 'repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/' in both git/refs/tags listing and per-tag ref resolution calls. No env var override or git remote derivation.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"If SCP is forked or operated under a different org, all --expected-wrapper-sha invocations fail with tag-not-found errors. Zero test coverage for non-canonical repo paths.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Replace literal with SCP_REPO=${SCP_REPO:-jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-} resolved once at script top. Preserves current behavior while allowing fork deployments to override.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\\n```\\\",\\\"stop_reason\\\":\\\"end_turn\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"c243b213-20ab-4743-9378-ce261044a917\\\",\\\"total_cost_usd\\\":1.3160887000000001,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":11,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":121712,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":553989,\\\"output_tokens\\\":46108,\\\"server_tool_use\\\":{\\\"web_search_requests\\\":0,\\\"web_fetch_requests\\\":0},\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":121712,\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0},\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"iterations\\\":[{\\\"input_tokens\\\":1,\\\"output_tokens\\\":8107,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":128613,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":480,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":480},\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\"}],\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"modelUsage\\\":{\\\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":1669,\\\"outputTokens\\\":30,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":0,\\\"cacheCreationInputTokens\\\":0,\\\"webSearchRequests\\\":0,\\\"costUSD\\\":0.0018189999999999999,\\\"contextWindow\\\":200000,\\\"maxOutputTokens\\\":32000},\\\"claude-sonnet-4-6\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":11,\\\"outputTokens\\\":46108,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":553989,\\\"cacheCreationInputTokens\\\":121712,\\\"webSearchRequests\\\":0,\\\"costUSD\\\":1.3142697,\\\"contextWindow\\\":200000,\\\"maxOutputTokens\\\":32000}},\\\"permission_denials\\\":[],\\\"terminal_reason\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"fast_mode_state\\\":\\\"off\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"4d2d9a12-7c20-4bce-8b85-3b0aec15d683\\\"}\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:1:# WP-SCP-024 024B-extras — CI wiring for the invocation-log gate.\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:2:#\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:3:# D-047 ratifies the break-glass restore flow and this workflow wiring.\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:4:# Plan-doc invariant 2 still governs the enforcement script itself;\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:5:# this workflow just feeds it the correct slice-local arguments.\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:6:#\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:7:# Critical bootstrap guard: paths-ignore excludes 024A / 024B-*\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:8:# tooling slices so the workflow does not self-trigger on the slice\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:9:# that introduced it.\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:10:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:11:name: check-invocation-log-entry\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:12:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:13:\\\"on\\\":\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:14:  pull_request:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:15:    branches: [main]\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:16:    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:17:    paths:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:18:      - \\\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**\\\"\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:19:      - \\\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md\\\"\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:20:      - \\\"STATUS.md\\\"\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:21:    paths-ignore: [\\\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**\\\"]\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:22:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:23:permissions:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:24:  contents: read\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:25:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:26:jobs:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:27:  check-invocation-log-entry:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:28:    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:29:    steps:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:30:      - name: Checkout repository\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:31:        uses: actions/checkout@de0fac2e4500dabe0009e67214ff5f5447ce83dd # v6.0.2\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:32:        with:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:33:          fetch-depth: 0\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:34:          persist-credentials: false\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:35:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:36:      - name: Resolve dispatch note path\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:37:        shell: bash\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:38:        run: |\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:39:          set -euo pipefail\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:40:          dispatch_note=\\\"$(git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD -- 'docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024*/DISPATCH-NOTE.md' | head -n1)\\\"\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:41:          if [ -z \\\"$dispatch_note\\\" ]; then\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:42:            echo \\\"error: could not resolve a dispatch note path from the PR diff\\\" >&2\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:43:            exit 1\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:44:          fi\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:45:          printf 'dispatch_note=%s\\\\n' \\\"$dispatch_note\\\" >> \\\"$GITHUB_ENV\\\"\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:46:\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:47:      - name: Check invocation log entry\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:48:        shell: bash\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:49:        run: |\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:50:          set -euo pipefail\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:51:          scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh \\\\\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:52:            --diff-base origin/main \\\\\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:53:            --dispatch-note \\\"$dispatch_note\\\" \\\\\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:54:            --status-md STATUS.md \\\\\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:55:            --branch-protection-log docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:1:# DISPATCH-NOTE — WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-extras\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:2:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:3:**Date:** 2026-05-10\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:4:**Branch:** `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras` (off main, after 024B-core merges)\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:5:**Predecessor:** WP-SCP-024 024B-core (merged at 249aa9f). Original 024B work preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking`. Split per `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md`.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:6:**Successor target:** WP-SCP-024 024C PIM canary cascade.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:7:**Decision filed:** D-047.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:8:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:9:`cascade-status: not applicable` — this slice ships rollback + break-glass + CI wiring; not a cohort cascade slice.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:10:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:11:## Backstory\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:12:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:13:024B-core merged at 249aa9f shipped scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + cascade-status CI enforcement script (CLI) + tests. This slice (024B-extras) ships the deferred deliverables.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:14:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:15:Carry-forward findings from extras-parking R8-archive (preserved in `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking`):\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:16:- **R8-CORR-001** (extras-parking): cascade-status regex first-match captures trailing inline prose. **CLOSED in 024B-core** via single-pass regex with full-value capture + closed-set validation.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:17:- **R8-CORR-002** (extras-parking): prior-entry detection runs outside restore-mode guard, emitting spurious contradiction message. **APPLIES TO 024B-EXTRAS** — ensure restore-mode guard scoping is tight.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:18:- **R8-CORR-003** (extras-parking): TF-ticket match pattern parameterises over canonicalised slug instead of plan-doc §2 invariant 2 literal regex. **CLOSED in 024B-core** (slug canonicalisation now spec-compliant).\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:19:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:20:## Why\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:21:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:22:024B-core delivered the WHAT (scaffolder + template + CI script + tests). This slice delivers the HOW (rollback + break-glass + CI integration):\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:23:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:24:1. **`enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode** proves invariant 7's <30-min rollback SLO is real, not aspirational. Operator-interactive demo at step 7 is merge-blocking AC and is recorded through the placeholder evidence path until the operator completes the real-repo round-trip.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:25:2. **ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure** documents the 3-gate playbook for federation-primitive failure recovery.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:26:3. **`.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`** wires the CLI script (shipped in 024B-core) into GitHub Actions so cohort cascade slices 024C–F have automated CI enforcement.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:27:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:28:Without 024B-extras, 024C cannot open. Plan-doc §6 cohort dispatcher precondition: 024C entry gates on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merging + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:29:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:30:## Scope (in)\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:31:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:32:| Deliverable | Path | Notes |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:33:|---|---|---|\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:34:| `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` (modify) | New `--restore <pre-state.json>` flag reverses prior branch-protection mutation per plan-doc invariant 7. Existing forward-mode unchanged. **Key behaviours per extras-parking lessons:** (a) GET-shape JSON transformed to PUT-shape via Python helper (strips `_links`, `url`, `checks`, `required_signatures`); (b) `required_signatures` reset via dedicated DELETE/POST sub-resource calls; (c) APPLY_FAIL=0 wrap pattern (failed PUT continues to log emission); (d) posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement` + `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks` required when before-state has `enforce_admins.enabled=false` or empty `required_status_checks.contexts`; (e) restore log block captures actual pre-restore state via `gh api -X GET` BEFORE PUT (not just the target good-state). |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:35:| Forward-mode safety check | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` (modify) | Refuses forward-mode invocation against repo with no successful `policy-check` workflow run on default branch in last 60 days. **Critical (R8 + R9 lessons):** workflow lookup by `path == \\\".github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml\\\"` (NOT by display name); query workflow-runs API WITHOUT `&branch=` filter (PR-triggered runs have head-branch = feature branch, not default; branch filter defeats gate). `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag for cold-start. |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:36:| `--expected-wrapper-sha` flag | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` (modify) | Validates supplied SHA against actual git tags via `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/git/ref/tags/<tag>` (NOT just 40-char shape match). Used by Gate 3 of break-glass. **Mutex with `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci`** (R7 SAFE-MAJ-001 closure). |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:37:| ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure | `docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md` (modify) | New §12.8 (between §12.7.15 and §13). 3-gate playbook: Gate 1 (DISABLE via `--restore` capturing pre-break SHA); Gate 2 (FIX via SHA-pin to last known-good release tag — concrete `gh api .../tags/<tag>` resolution; NOT illustrative); Gate 3 (RE-ENABLE via Renovate-bumped fix release + `--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha>` REQUIRED — not optional/advisory). SLO <30 min from operator decision to merge-restored state. WARNING + CAUTION callouts for `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` escape hatch. |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:38:| `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` | NEW file | CI workflow wiring for the CLI script (shipped in 024B-core). Triggers on `pull_request: [opened, synchronize, reopened]` against main with path filter targeting `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` + `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` + `STATUS.md`. **paths-ignore: `['docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**']`** to exclude tooling slices (024A plan-doc, 024B-core, 024B-extras themselves) — closes the bootstrap defect from extras-parking R7. SHA-pinned actions (per D-038 supply-chain hardening). Single job invokes `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh --diff-base origin/main --dispatch-note <found> --status-md STATUS.md --branch-protection-log docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`. Required-status-check eligible. |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:39:| `--restore` mode tests | `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` (modify) | Add `run_restore_case` + `make_restore_fake_gh` helpers (mirrors extras-parking patterns). Tests: GET→PUT shape transform; APPLY_FAIL pattern (failed PUT still emits log); posture-degradation flag enforcement; `required_signatures` POST + DELETE sub-resource handling; absolute path normalisation; --expected-wrapper-sha tag-validation (release-tag SHA → exit 0; arbitrary SHA → exit 2); --restore + forward-mode-flag incompatibility (--no-enforce-admins, --plan, --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate, --expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci). |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:40:| D-047 row | `docs/DECISIONS.md` | New decision ratifying --restore mode operational contract + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure + CI workflow wiring. |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:41:| STATUS.md update | `STATUS.md` | \\\"Today's chain (2026-05-10 — slice 024B-extras)\\\" entry. |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:42:| **Step 7 operator-interactive demo evidence** | `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md` | **MERGE-BLOCKING.** Operator-interactive after R-fixpoint reached. Real-repo round-trip on throw-away test repo: create test repo → invoke `enable-required-check.sh` forward-mode → capture pre-state → invoke `--restore` mode → verify branch-protection API response matches captured before-state byte-for-byte → commit evidence. NOT a dry-run mock. The placeholder path is the handoff target until the operator completes the demo. Closes plan-doc invariant 7 SLO + 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003. |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:43:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:44:## Scope (out)\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:45:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:46:- 024C PIM cascade kickoff. Unblocked when this slice merges + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closes.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:47:- TF-023E-002 closure. Carry-forward.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:48:- D-021 May-31 atomic-workday filing. Independent track.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:49:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:50:## Carry-forward known findings (from extras-parking r8-archive)\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:51:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:52:These were surfaced in extras-parking R8 but not closed at parking time. Address proactively in this slice:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:53:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:54:1. **R8-SAFE-001** (extras-parking): `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` is a backdoor; D-044 trust-model claim 'Gate 2 wrapper-SHA pin is explicit operator consent' becomes inaccurate when bypassed. Mitigation: WARNING + CAUTION callouts in ADOPT-001 §12.8 + log-block CAUTION line + D-047 rationale acknowledging escape hatch.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:55:2. **R8-SAFE-002** (extras-parking): Gate 3 forward-mode prior-entry detection misses uncommitted Gate-1 entries. Mitigation: also check working-tree diff via `git diff HEAD branch-protection-log.md`.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:56:3. **R8 Bootstrap** (extras-parking): workflow self-blocks introducing slice's own PR. Mitigation: paths-ignore `024[AB]*/**` in workflow path filter.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:57:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:58:## Acceptance criteria\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:59:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:60:- [ ] `--restore` mode logic correct (GET→PUT transform; APPLY_FAIL; posture-degradation flags; required_signatures sub-resource; pre-restore state capture; restore log block).\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:61:- [ ] Forward-mode safety check uses path-pinned workflow lookup (not display name) + no branch filter on workflow-runs API.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:62:- [ ] `--expected-wrapper-sha` validates against git tags (not just shape).\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:63:- [ ] ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure: 3-gate playbook with REQUIRED (not advisory) prerequisite checks; concrete tag-SHA resolution commands; WARNING + CAUTION callouts for escape hatches.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:64:- [ ] `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires CLI script with paths-ignore for 024[AB]*/** + SHA-pinned actions.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:65:- [ ] Tests cover all `--restore` mode behaviours + forward-mode safety check + workflow integration.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:66:- [ ] D-047 filed.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:67:- [ ] **Operator-interactive `--restore` real-repo round-trip demo evidence committed** (`docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md`).\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:68:- [ ] 3-lens R1+R2 fixpoint (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ).\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:69:- [ ] CI green.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:70:- [ ] Self-merge per D-040.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:71:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:72:## Cross-repo coordination\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:73:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:74:None for 024B-extras. Cascade-start announcement files at 024C kickoff per plan-doc §5.5.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:75:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:76:## FLA pilot safety findings reviewed\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:77:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:78:none new since 2026-05-09 — internal slice; no FLA implications.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:79:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:80:## Protocol deviation note\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:81:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:82:Same deviation as 024B-core: direct `codex exec` / `claude -p` (kernel hook in ACC only; FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 still open). Compensating manual steps apply.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:83:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:84:## Sequencing\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:85:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:86:| Phase | Work | Mode | Wall |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:87:|---|---|---|---|\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:88:| 0 | DISPATCH-NOTE finalised + spec_paths verified | Opus | done (this draft) |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:89:| 1 | Codex executor: --restore mode + safety check + --expected-wrapper-sha + ADOPT-001 §12.8 + workflow wiring + tests + D-047 + STATUS | Codex T3 | ~45 min |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:90:| 2 | Manual scope check + verify-commands | Opus | ~5 min |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:91:| 3 | 3× sequential Sonnet R1 review (64k cap) | Sonnet | ~30 min |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:92:| 4 | Fix-rounds (expected 1-2 given carry-forward findings pre-addressed) | Codex + Sonnet | variable |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:93:| 5 | **Operator-interactive `--restore` real-repo round-trip demo** | Operator interactive (gh PAT, throw-away test repo) | ~15 min |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:94:| 6 | Final R-fixpoint + self-merge | Opus | ~10 min |\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:95:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:96:Target: 024B-extras merged within ~3-4 hours wall-clock + operator demo gating window.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:97:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:98:## Reservation guard\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:99:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:100:D-047 reserved for this slice. Codex must NOT assign D-047 to anything else.\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:101:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:102:---\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:103:\\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:104:**Status:** ACTIVE (post-024B-core merge). Awaiting operator-interactive step-7 evidence completion and R-fixpoint review.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:1:# SCP Federation Primitive — Versioning Contract\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:2:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:3:**Status:** active as of slice 020H.1 (2026-05-01).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:4:**Closes:** WP-SCP-020 §4 020H.1 sub-criteria (i) + (ii).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:5:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:6:---\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:7:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:8:## Scope\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:9:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:10:This document defines the semver contract that the SCP federation\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:11:primitive guarantees to adopters who pin a `# tag: v<X>.<Y>.<Z>`\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:12:wrapper at `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml`. It covers three\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:13:public surfaces:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:14:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:15:1. **Reusable workflow inputs** — `workflow_call.inputs` declared on\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:16:   `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml`.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:17:2. **Schema contracts** — JSON Schema at\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:18:   `schemas/policy-check-summary.schema.json` (the structured\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:19:   summary artefact every adopter consumes for nightly + release-gate\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:20:   reconciliation), `schemas/rule-config.schema.json`, and\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:21:   `schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` (the opt-in cross-repo\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:22:   scorecard emit per WP-SCP-023 023B / D-041 — added at v1.2.0;\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:23:   MAJOR-pinned per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc §10 Q1).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:24:3. **Rule IDs** — the `SCP-R-NNN` identifiers under `policies/`.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:25:4. **Opt-in workflow inputs** — `scorecard-emit: bool` (added at\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:26:   v1.2.0 per WP-SCP-023 023B; default false). Opt-in inputs follow\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:27:   the same MINOR/MAJOR semver category as core inputs.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:28:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:29:It does NOT cover internal-only surfaces: `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh`,\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:30:`scripts/scp-policy-check.lock`, helper scripts in `scripts/`, the\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:31:Renovate preset internal shape, the OPA Rego `scp_common.rego`\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:32:helpers, or the SCP-self cross-repo aggregator pipeline\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:33:(`.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml`,\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:34:`schemas/scorecard-opt-in-registry.schema.json`,\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:35:`schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`,\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:36:`docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml`,\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:37:`output/scorecards/index.json` — added in slice 023C / D-042; mirrors\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:38:`.github/workflows/conflict-gate.yml` posture per slice 020N).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:39:These are refactored without notice.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:40:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:41:---\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:42:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:43:## Semver guarantee\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:44:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:45:**`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`** with strict semantic-versioning meaning:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:46:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:47:| Bump | When | Adopter action required |\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:48:|---|---|---|\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:49:| **PATCH** (`v1.0.x`) | Bug fixes, new informational annotations, performance improvements, observability records, internal refactors of helpers/lib. | None — drop in the SHA bump and merge. |\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:50:| **MINOR** (`v1.x.0`) | New `workflow_call` inputs (with safe defaults), new `SCP-R-NNN` rules added with `threshold: warn` baseline, new optional schema fields, new commit-status contexts (informational), new `disabled_rules:` reasons. | Recommended: review the release notes for new rules. None mandatory unless the adopter wants to opt into a new rule's `threshold: deny`. |\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:51:| **MAJOR** (`vX.0.0`) | Breaking changes — see \\\"What is breaking\\\" below. | **Mandatory** — read the migration guide in the release notes; an amending decision row in adopter's `DECISIONS.md` (or equivalent) before bumping the SHA pin. |\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:52:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:53:---\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:54:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:55:## What counts as a breaking change\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:56:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:57:Any of the following requires a MAJOR bump and an amending decision row:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:58:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:59:### Workflow inputs\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:60:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:61:- Removing a `workflow_call.inputs.<name>`.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:62:- Renaming a `workflow_call.inputs.<name>`.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:63:- Changing the `default:` value of an input in a way that flips an existing adopter's effective behaviour (e.g. `threshold: warn` → `threshold: deny`).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:64:- Changing the `type:` of an input.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:65:- Making a previously-optional input required.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:66:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:67:### Schema contracts\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:68:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:69:- Removing a previously-required field from `policy-check-summary.schema.json` or `rule-config.schema.json`.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:70:- Renaming any field (use add-new-then-deprecate instead).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:71:- Tightening a string `pattern:` such that previously-valid values are rejected.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:72:- Tightening a `format:` constraint (e.g. `date` → `date-time`).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:73:- Adding a new required field (covered by the deprecation ramp — see below).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:74:- Removing an `enum:` value that was previously emitted.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:75:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:76:### Rule IDs\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:77:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:78:- Removing an `SCP-R-NNN` rule.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:79:- Re-numbering an `SCP-R-NNN` rule (the ID is the durable contract; the underlying logic is internal).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:80:- Promoting a rule from `threshold: warn` to `threshold: deny` as the **default** at the SCP source. (Adopters may always override per-rule via `.scp/rule-config.yaml`; the default flip is what's breaking.)\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:81:- Tightening a rule's match scope such that previously-passing manifests now deny.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:82:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:83:### Read-back / annotation contracts\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:84:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:85:- Removing `scp/policy-check-readback` commit-status posting.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:86:- Removing a `::warning::` or `::error::` annotation surface that adopters' downstream tooling parses (e.g. an annotation parser that grouped on `title=SCP-E001`).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:87:- Renaming an `SCP-ENNN` error-code identifier.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:88:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:89:### Branch-protection helper\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:90:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:91:- Removing `--repo`, `--branch`, `--plan`, `--no-enforce-admins`, or `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` flags from `scripts/enable-required-check.sh`.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:92:- Changing the script's invocation-log markdown block schema.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:93:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:94:### Tag protection\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:95:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:96:- Changing the `v*` or `renovate/v*` Repository Ruleset shape (deletion / non-fast-forward / update behaviour).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:97:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:98:---\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:99:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:100:## What does NOT count as breaking\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:101:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:102:- Adding new `workflow_call.inputs.<name>` with a safe default.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:103:- Adding new `SCP-R-NNN` rules at `threshold: warn` baseline.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:104:- Adding new schema fields (`additionalProperties: false` is preserved — but new fields are added under existing properties, not as required new top-level fields).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:105:- Adding new `enum:` values that were not previously emitted.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:106:- Adding new `disabled_rules:` reasons.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:107:- Adding new informational `::warning::` or `::error::` titles (if existing titles preserved).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:108:- Internal helper-library refactors.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:109:- New commit-status contexts (the existing two are stable).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:110:- New OPA / Conftest / Regal binary version bumps in the lockfile (these are SHA-pinned; adopters get the new pins via Renovate auto-bump).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:111:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:112:---\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:113:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:114:## Deprecation ramp (one-release warning window)\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:115:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:116:**Closes 020H.1 sub-criterion (ii); enforced by 020H.3 release-gate.**\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:117:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:118:When the SCP source needs to remove or breaking-change one of the\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:119:public surfaces above, the change MUST proceed via a **one-release\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:120:deprecation ramp**:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:121:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:122:1. **Release N: add the new surface** (alongside the old surface), and\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:123:   in the same release add a `::warning::` annotation to the old\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:124:   surface stating: `<surface> deprecated; use <new-surface>; will be\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:125:   removed in v<X+1>.0.0`. Document in release notes. **Add an entry\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:126:   to `policies/deprecations.yaml`** with `announced_at`,\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:127:   `announced_release`, `target_release`, and `migration_pointer`\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:128:   (per `schemas/deprecations.schema.json`).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:129:2. **Release N+1 (the next MINOR or MAJOR — whichever lands first):**\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:130:   keep both surfaces live; the warning continues to fire.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:131:3. **Release N+M (the MAJOR after the next MINOR):** old surface is\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:132:   removed; the MAJOR bump is the breaking-change vehicle. An amending\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:133:   decision row in `docs/DECISIONS.md` records the removal. **Remove\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:134:   the entry from `policies/deprecations.yaml`** as part of the\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:135:   removal commit.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:136:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:137:The minimum gap between deprecation announcement (step 1) and\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:138:removal (step 3) is **one MINOR release**. Adopters who track every\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:139:MINOR release see at least one full PR cycle's worth of warnings\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:140:before the surface vanishes.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:141:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:142:**Machine enforcement** — two operating modes per `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml`:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:143:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:144:1. **Dry-run pre-flight (workflow_dispatch).** The pre-emptive\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:145:   enforcement path. The operator runs the gate BEFORE pushing the\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:146:   tag:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:147:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:148:   ```bash\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:149:   gh workflow run release-gate.yml -f dry_run_tag=v1.1.0\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:150:   # Wait for the run to start, then watch for completion + non-zero\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:151:   # exit on failure (gh run list always exits 0; gh run watch with\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:152:   # --exit-status surfaces the workflow's verdict). Closes 020H.3 R2\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:153:   # nit-SAFE-001.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:154:   sleep 5  # allow the dispatch to register\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:155:   RUN_ID=\\\"$(gh run list --workflow=release-gate.yml --limit 1 --json databaseId --jq '.[0].databaseId')\\\"\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:156:   gh run watch \\\"${RUN_ID}\\\" --exit-status\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:157:   ```\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:158:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:159:   If the dry-run exits clean, the tag is safe to push. **The\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:160:   dry-run pre-flight is mandatory before every v* tag-cut.**\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:161:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:162:2. **Post-tag observer (`push: tags: ['v*']`).** GitHub Actions\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:163:   cannot block a `push: tags` event — by the time the workflow\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:164:   fires, the tag already exists on the remote. This trigger\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:165:   therefore acts as a last-line-of-defense observer: it annotates\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:166:   the bad tag with `SCP-EREL-001` AND opens a\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:167:   `release-gate-violation` GitHub issue auto-assigned to `@jrnb2024`\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:168:   for triage (per slice 020H.3.1 closure of TF-020H3rg-003 —\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:169:   `permissions: { issues: write }` on the workflow + de-dup by tag,\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:170:   matching the canary-replay.yml pattern). The bad tag itself is\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:171:   immutable per D-030 (the `scp-tag-protection-v` Repository\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:172:   Ruleset blocks deletion + force-push + non-fast-forward, including\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:173:   for admins).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:174:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:175:Both modes evaluate the same TWO invariants:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:176:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:177:- any `policies/deprecations.yaml` entry has `target_release` matching\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:178:  the candidate tag AND `announced_release` is not at least one MINOR\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:179:  behind the candidate, OR\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:180:- any `.scp/rule-config.yaml` entry on the SCP repo itself has\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:181:  `disable: true` AND `expires_at < <UTC date>` (the SCP-self\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:182:  half of TF-005 — adopter-side rule-config expiry is enforced at\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:183:  PR time via SCP-E007, not here).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:184:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:185:The release-gate also emits **warning** annotations\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:186:(`SCP-EREL-001-warn`) on suspicious deprecation patterns\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:187:(announced_release more than one major behind candidate) without\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:188:blocking — operators triage manually.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:189:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:190:### Tag-cut procedure (operator)\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:191:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:192:Mandatory pre-flight + apply pattern. ALWAYS:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:193:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:194:1. **Author the release-prep PR.** Bump `version-manifest.json`;\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:195:   add or remove entries in `policies/deprecations.yaml` per the\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:196:   ramp; write release notes; merge to `main`.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:197:2. **Dry-run the gate.** `gh workflow run release-gate.yml -f dry_run_tag=<tag>` and wait for exit 0.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:198:3. **Push the tag.** Only after dry-run is clean. The post-tag\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:199:   observer fires automatically as a final check.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:200:4. **Publish the GitHub release** + Renovate bump cascade per the\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:201:   normal 020H part 2 procedure.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:202:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:203:### Bad-tag recovery procedure\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:204:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:205:If a tag is pushed that fails the post-tag observer:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:206:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:207:- **Do NOT attempt to delete or force-push the tag.** The D-030 +\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:208:  D-034 tag-protection rulesets block deletion and force-push,\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:209:  including for admins. The bad tag is immutable.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:210:- **Cut a corrected `v<X>.<Y+1>.0`** (next MINOR) that satisfies\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:211:  the ramp. The bad tag remains in the tag list but is superseded\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:212:  by the corrected one.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:213:- **Add a release note on the bad tag's GitHub release page**\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:214:  documenting the violation + pointing adopters to the corrected\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:215:  tag. Detection latency depends on the adopter's bump path:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:216:  - **Renovate-using adopters** (the §12.7.2 recommended path) see\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:217:    the automated bump PR to `v<X>.<Y+1>.0` within hours of\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:218:    publication; the bump PR is the primary signal.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:219:  - **Manually SHA-pinning adopters** see no immediate signal at\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:220:    all. The `SCP-FRESH-001` freshness warning (ADOPT-001 §12.7.11)\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:221:    fires only when the wrapper is more than `freshness_warning_threshold_minor` (default 2) MINOR releases behind main HEAD —\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:222:    so an adopter pinned to the bad v<X>.<Y>.<Z> sees the warning\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:223:    only after `v<X>.<Y+3>.0` has been cut. Manual quarterly review\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:224:    of the SCP releases page (per the §12.7.11 manual fallback) is\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:225:    the supplementary signal for this cohort.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:226:- **In an emergency only** (e.g. the bad tag introduced a security\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:227:  vulnerability that publishing a corrected tag does not\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:228:  immediately mitigate), the temporary-ruleset-disable path is:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:229:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:230:  ```bash\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:231:  # 1. Discover the ruleset id.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:232:  gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/rulesets \\\\\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:233:    --jq '.[] | {id, name}'\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:234:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:235:  # 2. Delete the ruleset (requires administration:write PAT).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:236:  gh api -X DELETE repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/rulesets/<id>\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:237:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:238:  # 3. Delete the bad tag.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:239:  git push --delete origin v<X>.<Y>.<Z>\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:240:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:241:  # 4. Restore the ruleset (idempotent; reproduces the D-030 state).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:242:  bash scripts/configure-020j-protections.sh\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:243:  ```\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:244:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:245:  This bypasses the bus-factor-1 protection and MUST be paired with\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:246:  an amending decision row in `docs/DECISIONS.md` (closes 020H.3\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:247:  R2 COR-nit-002).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:248:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:249:Rule deprecation specifically: when an `SCP-R-NNN` rule is\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:250:deprecated:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:251:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:252:- The rule's deny continues to fire at its current `threshold:` value\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:253:  during the deprecation window.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:254:- **The rule's own Rego implementation** emits a per-PR\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:255:  `::warning::SCP-R-NNN deprecated; will be removed in v<X+1>.0.0; <migration-pointer>`\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:256:  annotation. There is no centralized emitter — each rule self-announces.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:257:  This is the `SCP-DEP-001` annotation class (registered in ADOPT-001\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:258:  §12.7.7); the deprecation-PR adds the warning emission alongside\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:259:  the existing rule logic and adds the matching entry to\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:260:  `policies/deprecations.yaml`.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:261:- The release-cut at v<X+1>.0.0 removes the rule from `policies/`\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:262:  AND removes the entry from `policies/deprecations.yaml`. The\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:263:  release-gate enforces this contract (refuses to cut the tag if\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:264:  the entry is still present and the ramp window hasn't elapsed).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:265:- A migration pointer (link to a rule-proposal-style amending document\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:266:  or a §M.N section of an ADR) MUST be in the warning annotation.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:267:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:268:Non-rule surfaces (workflow inputs, schema fields, annotation titles,\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:269:branch-protection helper flags, tag-protection patterns) follow the\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:270:same ramp pattern with surface-specific emission paths — the\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:271:`policies/deprecations.yaml` entry has `surface_kind` covering each\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:272:category. The emission responsibility belongs to the surface\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:273:maintainer (e.g. a workflow-input deprecation announces via a\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:274:deprecation log line in the workflow itself).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:275:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:276:---\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:277:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:278:## What \\\"stable\\\" means for v1.x\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:279:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:280:`v1.0.0` (cut 2026-04-30) is the first stable release. Until v2.0.0 is\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:281:cut:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:282:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:283:- The three rules `SCP-R-001`, `SCP-R-002`, `SCP-R-003` keep their IDs\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:284:  and (subject to the deprecation ramp) their behaviour shape.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:285:- The `workflow_call` inputs declared on `policy-check.yml` at v1.0.0\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:286:  remain stable.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:287:- The `schemas/policy-check-summary.schema.json` shape at v1.0.0\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:288:  remains stable.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:289:- The required-check context name `policy-check / scp/policy-check`\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:290:  (per D-033) remains stable.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:291:- The Renovate preset `extends:` shorthand\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:292:  `github>jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-//renovate/default` remains\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:293:  stable.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:294:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:295:When v2.0.0 is contemplated, the proposal lands as an ADR via the\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:296:rule-RFC process at `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/` (see that\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:297:directory's `README.md`).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:298:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:299:---\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:300:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:301:## What adopters SHOULD do on each bump type\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:302:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:303:- **PATCH (auto-bumped by Renovate):** review the diff in the bump PR\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:304:  for unexpected behavioural changes, then merge. Most patches require\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:305:  no other action.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:306:- **MINOR:** read release notes; if any new rule lands at\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:307:  `threshold: warn` baseline, decide whether to opt into `threshold: deny`\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:308:  via `.scp/rule-config.yaml` or wait for the rule to be promoted in a\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:309:  future release.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:310:- **MAJOR:** read the migration guide in the release notes; file an\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:311:  amending decision row in your repo's `DECISIONS.md` (or equivalent)\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:312:  before bumping the SHA pin; if your repo is part of an estate\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:313:  cascade (WP-SCP-024), coordinate the bump with the estate owner.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:314:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:315:---\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:316:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:317:## How to file an amending decision\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:318:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:319:When an adopter accepts a MAJOR bump or breaking change, the\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:320:amending decision row should follow the pattern in\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:321:`docs/DECISIONS.md`:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:322:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:323:```\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:324:| D-NNN | <date> | Adopt SCP federation primitive v<X>.0.0 — breaking changes <enumerate>. <Migration steps taken>. | ACCEPTED | <rationale> |\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:325:```\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:326:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:327:This creates a durable audit trail of the version-bump decision\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:328:chain. Symmetric with how SCP self files D-022 (initial adoption)\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:329:and would file an amending row for any future SCP-self v2.0.0 jump.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:330:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:331:---\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:332:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:333:## References\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:334:\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:335:- WP-SCP-020 plan §4 020H.1 — slice acceptance for this document.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:336:- ADOPT-001 §12.7 — adopter integration appendix.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:337:- `docs/DECISIONS.md` D-022 — initial federation primitive adoption.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:338:- `docs/DECISIONS.md` D-036 — VERSIONING.md + rule-RFC process ratification.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:339:- `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/README.md` — rule-RFC process for rule additions and proposed breaking changes.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:340:- `policies/deprecations.yaml` — live deprecation register (the data the release-gate workflow reads).\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:341:- `schemas/deprecations.schema.json` — schema for the register.\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:342:- `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` — the machine-enforced ramp + expired-config refusal at tag-cut.\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1:# Standards Control Plane — Decision Log\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:2:\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:3:**Last Updated:** 2026-05-10 (D-047 filed for WP-SCP-024 024B-extras; restore/break-glass/workflow wiring)\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:4:\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:5:> **D-021 reservation note (2026-04-28):** D-021 is reserved for the\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:6:> 2026-05-31 atomic workday filing per WP-SCP-019 hygiene response (PR\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:7:> #30, 2026-04-21). Codex executors running WP-SCP-022 implementation\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:8:> slices must NOT assign D-021 to any decision filed during the\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:9:> autonomous run. The WP-SCP-022 §4.7 gate-enforcement helper\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:10:> (`scripts/wp_scp_022_gate_check.sh --check-d021`) detects collisions.\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:11:\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:12:> **D-041 / D-042 / D-043 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 023A):**\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:13:> D-041 is reserved for WP-SCP-023 slice 023B (cross-repo scorecard data\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:14:> shape + opt-in adopter participation model). D-042 is reserved for\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:15:> slice 023C (aggregator pipeline trust model — GitHub Actions Artifact\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:16:> Attestation for adopter emits + SCP-side Ed25519 key registry).\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:17:> **Mandatory trust constraint on D-042 (closes 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001,\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:18:> per WP-SCP-023 §5 step 3):** the 023C aggregator MUST verify the\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:19:> `job_workflow_ref` OIDC claim in each artifact attestation against the\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:20:> SCP reusable workflow path AND SHA pin via `gh attestation verify\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:21:> --signer-workflow <owner>/<repo>/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<sha>`;\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:22:> OIDC JWKS signature verification alone is not sufficient.\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:23:> D-043 is reserved for slice 023D (MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard`\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:24:> shape + read-only contract). Codex executors dispatched for any\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:25:> WP-SCP-023 implementation slice must NOT assign D-041, D-042, or D-043\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:26:> to any other decision filed during that slice. The reservation pattern\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:27:> mirrors the D-021 guard above.\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:28:\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:29:> **D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 024A):**\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:30:> D-044 was reserved for WP-SCP-024 slice 024B (`scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh`\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:31:> = `SCP-073-scaffolder` operational contract + adopter-template versioning\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:32:> + invocation-log convention extension). It is now filed as ACCEPTED in\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:33:> 024B-core; the deferred 024B-extras surface carries the `--restore`\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:34:> rollback mode and workflow wiring. D-045 is reserved for slice 024C (estate\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:35:> cascade ordering canary-first per WP-SCP-024 §5.1, per-adopter\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:36:> onboarding contract per §5.2, post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:37:> week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle per invariant 8, cascade-slice rollback\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:38:> procedure per invariant 7). D-046 is reserved for slice 024G\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:39:> (estate-cascade Threshold A criteria + post-Threshold-A maintenance\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:40:> posture: recurring drift remediation, version-ramp coordination,\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:41:> departing-adopter procedure; decision on whether `scp.consult_estate_status`\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:42:> ships standalone or rolls into existing `consult_scorecard`). Codex\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:43:> executors dispatched for any WP-SCP-024 implementation slice must NOT\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:44:> assign D-044, D-045, or D-046 to any other decision filed during that\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:45:> slice. The reservation pattern mirrors the D-021 / D-041–043 guards\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:46:> above.\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:47:\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:48:| ID | Date | Decision | Status | Rationale |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:49:|----|------|----------|--------|-----------|\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:50:| D-001 | 2026-04-11 | Use Python for the phase 1 CLI-first implementation | ACCEPTED | Fast path to explicit schemas, local tooling, JSON validation, and deterministic file-based execution |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:51:| D-002 | 2026-04-11 | Keep the project as a standalone app rather than extending docs-agent or Control Tower directly | ACCEPTED | Keeps evaluator runtime independent while still allowing later integration with both systems |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:52:| D-003 | 2026-04-11 | Limit the first governed implementation slice to standards registry loading, minimal findings loading, and consult retrieval | ACCEPTED | Keeps the first end-to-end work package narrow enough to review rigorously while still allowing real consult output |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:53:| D-004 | 2026-04-11 | Introduce an explicit project-area intermediate representation before evaluator implementation | ACCEPTED | Keeps evaluator inputs deterministic, testable, and independent from raw repo sprawl |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:54:| D-005 | 2026-04-11 | Wire governance evaluation through the audit CLI before attempting architecture evaluation | ACCEPTED | Establishes one real evaluator path end to end before widening the audit surface |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:55:| D-006 | 2026-04-11 | Extend audit and project-area contracts before WP-SCP-003 implementation | ACCEPTED | Governance review evidence and unsupported-domain coverage must be first-class structured data, not implied by prose or raw path scanning |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:56:| D-007 | 2026-04-11 | Use an explicit unattended-delivery protocol for the remaining programme | ACCEPTED | The remaining work should continue without waiting for user answers, using documented default decisions, bounded review loops, and backlog carry-forward for non-blocking residuals |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:57:| D-008 | 2026-04-12 | Use explicit file-content signal heuristics for phase-1 architecture evaluation | ACCEPTED | The architecture slice needs deterministic, test-backed checks against repo-local evidence rather than broad semantic inference or prompt-only judgement |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:58:| D-009 | 2026-04-12 | Add a second repo-backed fixture corpus for architecture signal coverage | ACCEPTED | `ARCH-003` and `ARCH-004` need concrete repo-backed sample files instead of synthetic payload-only tests if the slice is going to prove its own honesty |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:59:| D-010 | 2026-04-12 | Reconcile findings by deterministic finding ID and area-scoped audit coverage | ACCEPTED | Findings persistence must refresh and resolve records only inside the audited area and evaluated domains so unrelated history is not disturbed |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:60:| D-011 | 2026-04-12 | Guard findings persistence with scope-collision checks and per-file atomic replacement plus rollback | ACCEPTED | Persisted lifecycle state must fail on `finding_id` scope collisions and should avoid half-written files without pretending phase 1 has a crash-safe multi-file transaction |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:61:| D-012 | 2026-04-12 | Bind generated report and area-summary timestamps to the current audit timestamp | ACCEPTED | Report outputs need byte-stable reruns and freshness checks, so they should reuse `audit_result.generated_at` rather than inventing wall-clock timestamps |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:62:| D-013 | 2026-04-12 | Reuse the current write-flow guarantees for report artifacts and carry true bundled transactions to backlog | ACCEPTED | The reporting slice should stay downstream of the existing persistence guarantees instead of pretending to offer a crash-safe cross-artifact commit in phase 1 |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:63:| D-014 | 2026-04-12 | Guard `report` freshness with embedded findings-state signatures as well as audit timestamp | ACCEPTED | A date-bound audit timestamp alone is too weak to detect same-day content drift, so the report needs a stronger freshness check against persisted findings state |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:64:| D-015 | 2026-04-12 | Apply waivers as an audit-time overlay rather than embedding waiver rules inside evaluators | ACCEPTED | Evaluators should keep emitting deterministic raw findings so the same checks can be reused with or without waivers, while audit assembly owns exception handling |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:65:| D-016 | 2026-04-12 | Centralise score calculation in a shared module and count only active unwaived findings against score | ACCEPTED | Score semantics must be documented, deterministic, and consistent across evaluators and audit assembly, and waived issues should not drag active score down |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:66:| D-017 | 2026-04-12 | Use one embedded fenced JSON review-evidence block as the shared contract for governance validation and historical review retrieval | ACCEPTED | One small structured block inside markdown keeps review evidence inspectable in git while avoiding two drifting review-data formats |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:67:| D-018 | 2026-04-12 | Keep historical review retrieval as explicit consult output rather than hiding it inside generic guidance text | ACCEPTED | Review history should be visible, bounded, and machine-readable so later consumers can use it without reparsing prose |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:68:| D-019 | 2026-04-18 | SVC-003 is declare-a-contract with a closed four-mode set (`mode.user_oidc`, `mode.service_rs256`, `mode.api_key`, `mode.bearer_legacy`); commit `66ba8a4` codifies `mode.user_oidc` with no rework; WP-SCP-018 `--auth-token` classifies as `mode.bearer_legacy` with deprecation close date 2026-06-30 | ACCEPTED | Estate reality has three live token types plus a cookie session flow; a single fixed mechanism breaks machine callers; a closed mode set prevents drift; codifying the existing CT OIDC layer keeps the in-repo auth story consistent without forcing a rework |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:69:| D-020 | 2026-04-18 | `_normalise_scope` accepts `request.scope.area_id` as the normaliser hint when `_infer_area_id` raises `AreaIdInferenceError`; mismatched-inference still raises the same way as before | ACCEPTED | Adopters auditing scopes that lack an ENH-style marker (e.g. a root-level `services.yml` dogfood) would otherwise have to plant placeholder enhancement docs to satisfy area-id inference; the narrow relaxation preserves the auditor discipline of catching inferred-vs-claimed mismatches while closing the genuine uninferrable-scope ergonomic gap |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:70:| D-022 | 2026-04-21 | Adopt reusable GitHub Actions workflow + OPA/Conftest + Renovate shared preset + required status check with `enforce_admins=true` as the estate's policy federation primitive. Alternatives rejected: `palantir/policy-bot` (GitHub App per org, HCL-not-Rego, no Renovate cascade, no native waiver-overlay); custom control-plane service (build cost, duplicates GH Actions + branch protection primitives) | ACCEPTED | Industry-standard shape; no custom control-plane service required; cheapest path converting SCP from advisory auditor to pre-merge gate; Renovate preset cascade gives \\\"change one rule → enforce across 10 repos in 24h\\\"; supports waiver-aware evaluation and structured annotation payloads. Full rationale body in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §10 |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:71:| D-023 | 2026-04-21 | Reject multi-agent free-form chat-forum pattern as the agent-coordination venue; adopt structured proposal queue (`docs/reviews/proposals/PROP-NNN.md` + MCP `propose()` tool — initial stub in WP-SCP-021 slice 021E; full adjudication workflow in `WP-SCP-022-proposal-queue`, separately tracked per `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §12). Agents never free-form chat with each other; they read SCP's decision records and call SCP's MCP tools | ACCEPTED | Du et al. (ICML 2024, `arxiv 2305.14325`) show multi-agent debate converges to consensus fast including when the consensus is wrong; Anthropic's multi-agent research post reports ~15× token cost with compounding coordination errors; human-on-the-loop literature converges on moderator-as-bottleneck past a few decisions/hour. Proposal-queue pattern scales because the human is on the loop, not in it. Full rationale body in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §10 (decision originator) and `docs/plans/WP-SCP-021-scp-as-mcp-server.md` §10 (`propose()` stub design). Note 2026-04-28: original D-023 forward-referenced \\\"WP-SCP-022 plan when that WP opens\\\"; WP-SCP-022 v0.2 is the implementation programme plan, not the proposal-queue WP — the rationale-body expansion lives in the parent plans named here, and the adjudication WP is renamed `WP-SCP-022-proposal-queue` |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:72:| D-024 | 2026-04-21 | Adopt Anthropic's Model Context Protocol (MCP) as the estate's agent-to-SCP tool protocol. Transports: stdio (primary, local, trust-the-process) + streamable HTTP (opt-in, bearer-token via `SCP_MCP_TOKEN` with 30-day rotation overlap). Ed25519 asymmetric signing for consult receipts — SCP holds private key; adopters verify with public key published at `scp://security/signing-keys` + committed `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` (90-day rotation overlap). Python `mcp` SDK pinned by version + sdist SHA256; distributed via PyPI as `standards-control-plane[mcp]` extra. OAuth deferred to SCP-075-oauth | ACCEPTED | MCP is the dominant vertical agent-to-tool protocol post Linux Foundation Agentic AI Foundation launch (Dec 2025); Anthropic is protocol origin; Claude Code/Desktop + ACC speak MCP natively. Asymmetric signing prevents adopter-held-key forgery (HMAC symmetric rejected in adversarial review round 1). Alternatives rejected: raw REST (no client ecosystem); custom JSON-RPC (reinvents MCP); gRPC (no agent client support); HMAC symmetric (forgeable by any key-holding adopter). Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-021-scp-as-mcp-server.md` §10 |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:73:| D-025 | 2026-04-21 | Scoped pre-code consult requirement with Ed25519-signed receipts. Downstream `CLAUDE.md` mandates `scp.consult_rules` before code authoring in governed domains; Claude Code `PreCommit` hook refuses commit without valid receipt. Scope rule: hook consults `scp://rules/domain-map` via `resolve_domain(changed_files)`; non-empty result → receipt required; default-skip globs for docs-only changes. Receipt envelope binds `{schema_version, key_id, repo, head_sha, base_sha, changed_files_hash, domains_covered, issued_at, expires_at ≤ 2h}`; hook validates every field. Break-glass `SCP_MCP_ALLOW_OFFLINE=true` requires committed `docs/overrides/OVERRIDE-NNN.md` with schema-validated expiry ≤ 14d; emits tracked finding SCP-MCP-E010 | ACCEPTED | Client-side enforcement pairs with server-side gate (WP-SCP-020) as belt + braces; scoped + TTL + PR-bound receipts prevent replay/forgery/scope-bypass. Break-glass requires sibling OVERRIDE artefact so fail-closed posture is maintained. Rego gate is authoritative — MCP consult never bypasses. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-021-scp-as-mcp-server.md` §10 |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:74:| D-026 | 2026-04-28 | Autonomous-dispatch protocol for SCP implementation slices. Each WP-SCP-020 and WP-SCP-021 implementation slice flows through four-tier dispatch: Opus orchestrator (current agent) prepares dispatch package conforming to `~/Projects/acc/schemas/codex_work_package.schema.json`; Codex executor tier runs the slice via `codex_dispatch.py`; 3× parallel Sonnet R1 reviewers apply correctness / safety_bypass / completeness_governance lenses via `claude_dispatch.py` with 500 ms stagger; Opus consolidates verdicts and orchestrates fix rounds. Recurse to fixpoint per `feedback_recursive_adversarial_review.md`. Fix-round budget 5; on budget exhaustion, slice escalates to user review. Evidence persists at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/<slice-id>/`. No slice merges without 3× APPROVED verdict | ACCEPTED | Estate four-tier dispatch standard since 2026-04-22 (per `feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md`); applies to non-trivial work. SCP implementation slices are non-trivial — they touch CI, branch protection, signing keys, and PyPI. Adversarial review pattern proven on WP-SCP-019 (5 rounds), WP-SCP-020 (5 rounds), WP-SCP-021 (3 rounds, fixpoint). Persisting evidence in-repo gives a permanent audit trail and lets future agents recover from session-bounded amnesia. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4 |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:75:| D-027 | 2026-04-28 | Parallel-track execution for WP-SCP-020 (federation primitive) and WP-SCP-021 (MCP server) implementation, Scope Y per user 2026-04-28 selection. Both tracks run concurrently from dispatch-zero to user-gate. Track 1 (020): 020B → 020B.1 → 020B.2 → 020C → 020C.1 → 020J → 020K → 020D1 → 020H part 1 → 020E.a → [USER-GATE-A0 release sign-off] → 020H part 2 → 020D2 → [USER-GATE-A] (12 implementation slices + 1 mid-chain human-input gate + 1 terminal gate, matching WP-SCP-020 §3 canonical sequence verbatim). Track 2 (021): 021B → 021C → 021D → 021E → [USER-GATE-C] (4 implementation slices + 1 terminal gate). Concurrent-dispatch limit: 4 active Codex sessions across both tracks. `pyproject.toml` partition: Track 1 owns `[tool.scp.federation]` and adds `scp-policy-check` to `[project.scripts]`; Track 2 owns `[project.optional-dependencies.mcp]` and adds `scp-mcp-server` to `[project.scripts]`. `docs/STATUS.md` excluded from all slice scope_boundary globs | ACCEPTED | WP-SCP-021 §scope statement declares the tracks independent; serial execution would defer MCP availability for ~2× wall-clock without quality gain. Concurrent dispatch within rate-limit envelope per `four-tier-dispatch-field-report-2026-04-22.md`. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.4. Track 1 sequence corrected in v0.2 (R1 fix-round) to match WP-SCP-020 §3 canonical ordering — earlier draft omitted 020K and inverted 020D2 placement |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:76:| D-028 | 2026-04-28 | SCP adopts D-048 / ADR-016 Design Parity Build Method (DPBM) as a contract input for any SCP slice that produces designed visual output. Layered amendment to four-tier dispatch — prototype + flows + design principles enter the contract layer the build is bound to. Enforcement-injection mechanism per `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.6: visual-output slices' dispatch packages MUST include a \\\"DPBM contract\\\" subsection naming prototype path, flow diagram, and design-principles reference; orchestrator verifies subsection presence before launching the review pass; absence is treated as a CRIT finding. Within WP-SCP-022 itself no slices match the DPBM \\\"applies\\\" criteria (workflow / Rego / MCP-server / CI work, no visual output); D-028 is forward-looking. WP-SCP-024 estate cascade inherits D-028; FLA, ACC, RI canary-onboarding instructions reference the DPBM contract layer. D-028 lands operationally once CT PR #202 + ACC PR #106 have merged | ACCEPTED | DPBM closes a structural gap that pure-code lenses can't see — a frontend built under standard four-tier dispatch can satisfy every test and still drift from the design. Without an SCP-side adoption decision, agents working through SCP's MCP consult won't be told that the contract for visual-output work includes design artefacts. CT PR #202 + ACC PR #106 (both 2026-04-28) introduce the upstream doctrine; SCP adopts at the policy layer. Full rationale + injection-mechanism specification in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.6 |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:77:| D-029 | 2026-04-29 | `policy-check.yml` reusable workflow `permissions:` block expands to `contents: read, statuses: write` to support WP-SCP-022 020C.1(vi) read-back commit-status posting on the sibling context `scp/policy-check-readback`. Original 020B(iii) baseline was `contents: read` only. The `statuses: write` privilege uses the caller's `${{ github.token }}` and posts only to `repos/<caller>/statuses/${{ pull_request.head.sha }}`; no other write surface is unlocked. Disabling the read-back would require accepting a regression on 020C.1(vi); keeping `contents: read` only would prevent the read-back from being posted | ACCEPTED | The read-back surface is the only place a PR reviewer sees waiver/disabled-rule posture without reading JSON artefacts; WP-SCP-020 §4.3 fixpoint criteria for 020C.1(vi) require it. The privilege footprint is narrowest possible — `statuses: write` does not allow content modification, branch operations, issue/PR comments, or token impersonation. The workflow checkout uses `persist-credentials: false` so the elevated privilege is bounded to the policy-check job. Plan amendment: `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §4 020B(iii) updated with cross-reference to D-029. Identified by WP-SCP-022 R1 completeness review (MAJ-005) |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:78:| D-030 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020J on the SCP repository: (a) tag-protection rule on `v*` (legacy tag-protection API and/or Repository Ruleset) preventing force-push or deletion of release tags; (b) `required-signed-commits` on `main` so every commit reaching `main` carries a verified signature. Both are preconditions for slice 020D1 (self-dogfood wrapper pinned at the v1.0.0-rc.1 commit-SHA) and 020D2 (required-status-check + v1.0.0 cut). Configured via `scripts/configure-020j-protections.sh` (idempotent API caller). Documented in `docs/security/branch-protection.md`. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: a single GitHub admin (@jrnb2024) can disable these via repo Settings; quarterly review cadence per WP-SCP-020 §14 U-sec-2 closure | ACCEPTED | Path (a) selected at WP-SCP-020 plan merge per §14 U-sec-2 — Personal GitHub Pro tier supports both protections natively, no signed-release-manifest substitute needed. Tag-protection prevents tag mutation post-cut (the supply-chain anchor for adopters pinning by SHA + comment-tag); required-signed-commits prevents un-attested code from reaching the gate's source of truth. Future direct commits to main without a verified signature are blocked, which is the intent (forces all changes through PRs whose squash-merges are auto-signed by GitHub's bot key). The unsigned commit `bcfc706` (USER-GATE-C signoff, 2026-04-29, unsigned) predates this enablement and is grandfathered. Identified as gate-readiness work in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §4 020J + §3 sequence + §8 risks (\\\"Bootstrap trust\\\") + §9.1 sequencing |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:79:| D-031 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020K on the SCP repository in the personal-account / single-operator mode resolved at §14 U-k closure: (a) NO `scp-break-glass` GitHub team is created — GitHub teams are not available on user namespaces and `jrnb2024` is a personal user account; (b) `CODEOWNERS` extends to cover the additional governance-sensitive paths named in §4 020K (canonical-minimum), then broadened/extended via 020K R1+R2+R3 safety reviews to close 7 MAJ + 4 MIN + 6 nit findings — see CODEOWNERS file header + `FIX-ROUND-{1,2,3}.md` for the full audit trail of which paths were broadened (subsuming a narrower canonical rule) vs added net-new; (c) at slice 020D2, branch-protection on `main` is configured with `required_approving_review_count = 1`, `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`, and `require_review_from_non_author = false` (solo operator; self-approval is the only option) — **NOTE (D-033 amendment, 2026-04-30 evening):** the anticipated `required_approving_review_count = 1` was corrected to `count = 0` by D-033 when the first PR through enforced mode revealed that GitHub forbids PR self-review; count=1 + sole CODEOWNER = operator locked out of repo. See D-033 for the live state, the operational test path (USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64), and the second-maintainer escalation path; (d) §8 bus-factor-1 risk row remains LIVE with quarterly escalation review at 2026-07-21 named in `STATUS.md` \\\"Open scheduled follow-ups\\\" and in auto-memory `project_scheduled_followups.md`. **Escalation path when a second maintainer onboards:** add them to `CODEOWNERS`, flip `require_review_from_non_author = true`, amend §8 risk row to CLOSED. **020D1 → 020D2 dependency:** 020K completes before 020D2 opens (the branch-protection wiring at 020D2 reads from CODEOWNERS established here). Identified at WP-SCP-020 plan §3 sequence + §4 020K + §14 U-k closure | ACCEPTED | Personal-account path is the only viable shape for v1.0.0 on a personal user namespace. The CODEOWNERS expansion forces every future change to `renovate/**` (Renovate preset that cascades pin-bumps across adopters), `docs/DECISIONS.md` (the decision-record canonical home), and `output/findings/waivers.json` (the safety-valve store) through reviewer attention rather than allowing direct push. Bus-factor-1 is acknowledged as live operational exposure rather than papered over: `require_review_from_non_author = false` reflects reality (a solo operator cannot self-approve under non-author review), and the 2026-07-21 quarterly review is the named re-evaluation moment. Path (b) extension of `CODEOWNERS` is forward-looking on `renovate/**` (the directory does not yet exist in the working tree; it lands in slice 020F); CODEOWNERS rules on non-existent paths are no-ops, so adding the rule pre-emptively is harmless and removes a future drift risk where 020F could land without simultaneously adding the matching CODEOWNERS row. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §4 020K + §8 (bus factor risk row, line 188) + §14 U-k closure |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:80:| D-032 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020D2 on the SCP repository post-USER-GATE-A0: enable `scp/policy-check` as a required status check on `main` with `strict: true` (PR must be up-to-date with base before evaluation); set `enforce_admins: true` (no admin bypass); set `required_pull_request_reviews` with `required_approving_review_count: 1`, `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`, `require_code_owner_reviews: true`; explicitly leave `require_review_from_non_author: false` per 020K personal-account closure (single-operator self-approval is the only viable path). Configured via `scripts/configure-020d2-required-check.sh` (idempotent). After 020D2, every PR to `main` must pass the federation primitive's gate AND have at least one approving review AND have a verified signature on every commit AND cannot be bypassed by the admin role. The 020E.a pre-protection canary (workflow-run-id 25172373569) demonstrated the deny path on a real PR with a real violation pre-flip; 020E.b will demonstrate that the now-required check actually blocks merge. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: a single GitHub admin (@jrnb2024) is the operator; quarterly review at 2026-07-21 (per 020K + D-031) reconciles documented-vs-live state. **Note (D-033 forward-reference, 2026-04-30 evening):** the live state of three D-032 parameters was amended same-day by D-033 — the required-check context name corrected from `scp/policy-check` to `policy-check / scp/policy-check` (rendered Actions name); `required_approving_review_count` corrected from 1 to 0 (single-operator self-approval is structurally impossible on GitHub); `require_code_owner_reviews` corrected from true to false (same root cause). See D-033 for the operational test path that surfaced these | ACCEPTED | This is the operational closure of the WP-SCP-020 federation primitive — SCP gates itself on its own `main`. Closure of governance B-2 (the original brief was \\\"convert SCP from advisory auditor to deterministic pre-merge enforcement\\\"). Required-status-check + enforce_admins=true + required-signed-commits + required-PR-reviews compose into a 4-layer protection: (1) every commit is cryptographically attested, (2) every change runs through the SCP gate, (3) every change has at least one human approval, (4) admin override is OFF. Single-operator self-approval is the bus-factor-1 cost; the 2026-07-21 escalation review is the named re-evaluation moment. The pre-protection canary (020E.a) proved the deny mechanism worked on real PR; flipping to required adds enforcement, not behaviour. Identified at WP-SCP-020 plan §3 sequence + §4 020D2; preconditions 020J + 020K + 020D1 + 020E.a + USER-GATE-A0 all closed before this slice opens |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:81:| D-033 | 2026-04-30 | WP-SCP-022 020D2.1 reconciliation: amend D-032's branch-protection shape on the SCP repo to reflect two operational realities surfaced when the first PR (USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64) attempted to merge through enforced mode. (a) **Required-check context name correction:** WP-SCP-020 020B(xi) specified `scp/policy-check` as the context name. GitHub Actions renders the actual check-run as `<wrapper-workflow-name> / <reusable-job-name>` — for SCP self this is `policy-check / scp/policy-check`. The bare `scp/policy-check` context matches only the readback status posted by the reusable workflow's commit-status step, NOT the primary check-run from the wrapper. Required-check context updated to `policy-check / scp/policy-check`. (b) **Personal-account review-shape correction:** D-032 originally set `required_approving_review_count = 1` + `require_code_owner_reviews = true` per WP-SCP-020 020D2 spec. GitHub forbids PR authors from approving their own PRs. In single-operator mode with @jrnb2024 as the only maintainer AND only CODEOWNER, count=1 + codeowner=true locks the operator out of every PR; `enforce_admins=true` prevents `gh pr merge --admin` from bypassing. Updated to `count=0` + `codeowner_reviews=false` in single-operator mode. CODEOWNERS still serves as documentation of who SHOULD approve when a second maintainer arrives. Forward-looking discipline preserved: when a second maintainer onboards, flip count=1 + codeowner=true + non-author=true in one operation. Both corrections are landed in `scripts/configure-020d2-required-check.sh` (idempotent re-run reproduces the live state) + `docs/security/branch-protection.md` + WP-SCP-020 §8 risk row. The 2026-07-21 quarterly escalation review re-evaluates the personal-account shape | ACCEPTED | First-PR-through-enforcement is the operational test of the spec; the test surfaced two assumptions that didn't survive contact with GitHub's actual behaviour: (1) the bare context name from 020B(xi) was incomplete (didn't anticipate Actions' `<workflow> / <job>` rendering for reusable-workflow callers), and (2) \\\"self-approval is the only option\\\" in 020K's wording was operationally impossible (GitHub forbids PR self-review). Both corrections are operational closure of the spec gap; neither weakens the security posture. The 4-layer protection (signed commits + required check + no admin bypass + tag protection) remains intact. The review-count=0 acceptance is the explicit bus-factor-1 cost; review enforcement returns the moment a second maintainer joins. Identified by USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64's failed merge attempt 2026-04-30 |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:82:| D-034 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020F renovate-tag-protection (parallel ruleset to D-030's `v*` ruleset, targeting `refs/tags/renovate/v*`). Closes 020F R1 safety review CRIT-SAFE-001: `renovate/v*` tag series unprotected — an attacker with push access could silently re-point `renovate/v1.0.0` to a malicious commit and cascade adversarial Renovate config to every estate adopter on their next scheduled run. The 020J ruleset matches `refs/tags/v*` (literal v-prefix at start) only. New ruleset `scp-tag-protection-renovate-v` applies same protections (deletion / non_fast_forward / update blocked, `enforcement: active`, `bypass_actors: []`). Configured via `scripts/configure-020f-renovate-tag-protection.sh` (idempotent, jq-based JSON construction to eliminate heredoc-interpolation injection surface, multi-property post-creation verification). Documented in `docs/security/branch-protection.md` \\\"Tag protection — renovate/v* pattern\\\" section. Symmetric with D-030 in posture and rationale; the only material difference is the tag-pattern segment. The `renovate/v*` series carries equal supply-chain weight as `v*` because every adopter that extends the preset cascades changes from the renovate-pattern tag to their own gate config | ACCEPTED | The 020J ruleset's `v*` literal-prefix pattern is by-design narrow; broadening to all release-track tags would require a separate ruleset per pattern. Renovate's preset shorthand `github>jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-//renovate/default#renovate/v1.0.0` is the standard Renovate adopter onboarding shape; without ruleset protection, the entire preset trust chain is rooted in mutable tag refs. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged identically to D-030: the same admin who owns @jrnb2024 is the one publishing tags; the protection guards against accidental force-push, not against malicious admin action. Quarterly review cadence (2026-07-30 in STATUS.md \\\"Open scheduled follow-ups\\\") covers both rulesets together. Identified by 020F R1 safety review (workflow run dispatched 2026-04-30 evening) — surfaced under the no-silent-descope governance invariant after fix-round-1 closed the substantive R1 findings |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:83:| D-035 | 2026-04-30 | Adopt the WP-SCP-020 slice 020G adopter-helper invocation procedure as estate doctrine. The required-check context name `policy-check / scp/policy-check` traces to D-033 (the rendered Actions check-run name established for the SCP self-dogfood gate). Adopters of the SCP federation primitive enable this required status check on their default branch via `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` from the SCP repo. The script applies branch protection in two API calls (unified PUT for status-checks/admins/reviews + dedicated POST to `required_signatures` sub-resource per the GitHub API shape), refuses to bypass admin enforcement without an explicit `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` acknowledgement flag, refuses to run in CI (CI=true / GITHUB_ACTIONS=true env-var guards), preserves any pre-existing `required_pull_request_reviews` shape rather than nulling it, and emits an invocation-log block (operator, timestamp, script SHA256 + git SHA, target repo+branch, before/after API JSON) for paste into `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`. The log commit is part of the invocation procedure: an apply without the log entry is considered unrecorded. Estate cascade rollout (WP-SCP-024) drives this script across PIM, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower; FLA pilot (WP-SCP-020.1) is the canary first invocation | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-030 (020J `v*` tag-protection), D-031 (020K CODEOWNERS personal-account), D-032 (020D2 SCP-self required-status-check), D-034 (020F `renovate/v*` tag-protection): every operational procedure that mutates third-party repository state ships an idempotent applier + ratifying D-NNN + invocation log convention. The bootstrap-only / no-CI guard reflects that this script writes to a third-party repo's branch protection — an automation tool that ran it unattended could mass-mutate the estate via stolen credentials before any operator noticed. The `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` confirmation reflects that `--no-enforce-admins` defeats the whole point of the federation primitive on the target repo and so should require explicit intent. The `required_pull_request_reviews` preservation reflects that adopters with multi-maintainer teams have legitimate review-shape state that 020G must not destroy. Identified at WP-SCP-020 §4 020G + 020G R1 review (3 MAJ + 5 MIN + 2 nit on safety, 2 MAJ + 4 MIN + nit on completeness, 3 MAJ + 2 MIN + 2 nit on correctness — fixpoint via fix-round-1) |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:84:| D-036 | 2026-05-01 | Adopt `policies/VERSIONING.md` MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH semver contract on the SCP federation primitive's public surfaces (`workflow_call.inputs` on `policy-check.yml`, `schemas/policy-check-summary.schema.json` + `schemas/rule-config.schema.json`, `SCP-R-NNN` rule IDs) WITH a one-release deprecation ramp before any breaking change AND `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/` RFC-lite process (quorum=1 SCP-CODEOWNER per D-031 single-operator mode; 48h wall-clock window with weekend-counts; 0 approvals = auto-defer with `defer` label; bypass-introducing proposals require explicit §5 enumeration and a non-waivable 48h window per 020H.1 R1 SAFE-MAJ-001 closure) as estate doctrine for SCP federation primitive versioning and rule governance. Closes WP-SCP-020 §4 020H.1 (i)+(ii)+(iii) and BS-5. Forward-compat to 2-of-N quorum when a second maintainer onboards (D-031 escalation path, 2026-07-21 review). Internal-only surfaces (`lib/policy_check_invocation.sh`, `scripts/scp-policy-check.lock`, helper scripts in `scripts/`, Renovate preset internal shape, OPA Rego helpers in `policies/scp_common.rego`) are explicitly NOT covered — they may be refactored without notice | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-035 (020G adopter-helper invocation): every new governance procedure binding adopter behaviour ships a ratifying D-NNN row to make the doctrine searchable in the canonical decision-record home rather than buried in a slice DISPATCH-NOTE. The one-release deprecation ramp is the MINIMUM version-skew adopters must tolerate before a surface vanishes; combined with the Renovate preset's automated SHA-pin bumps, this gives every adopter at least one full PR cycle's worth of warning annotations before a breaking change lands. The RFC-lite process is intentionally lightweight at v1.0.0 because the SCP estate is single-operator; the auto-defer mechanism is currently a manual close + label step. As estate scale grows (WP-SCP-024 cascade), the auto-defer mechanism may be lifted to a GitHub Action that runs on a schedule. Identified at WP-SCP-020 §4 020H.1 plan row + 020H.1 R1 completeness COMP-MAJ-003 closure |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:85:| D-037 | 2026-05-01 | Grant `issues: write` permission to the `release-gate-violation-issue` job in `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` (per WP-SCP-022 020H.3.1, closing TF-020H3rg-003). Privilege scope is the JOB level (not workflow default); the release-gate evaluation job continues to run with `contents: read` only. The new job fires only on `needs.release-gate.result == 'failure' && github.event_name == 'push'` — workflow_dispatch dry-runs and clean push:tags runs never reach it. The job's only mutation is `gh issue create` / `gh issue comment` / `gh label create --force` against the SCP source repo's own Issues namespace; no other write surface is unlocked. The auto-opened issue assigns `@jrnb2024` (single-operator mode per D-031); forward-compat env `SCP_RELEASE_GATE_ASSIGNEES` for 2nd-maintainer escalation. Symmetric with D-029 (020C.1 `statuses: write` for read-back commit-status) — a privilege-write expansion ratified by an amending decision row that names the precise threat-surface and bounded behaviour | ACCEPTED | The release-gate's last-line-of-defense alarm needs SOME write surface to surface beyond the workflow log; opening a GitHub issue is the lightest-weight signal that survives operator absence (the workflow log is ephemeral; the issue persists + assigns + sends a notification). Privilege-of-least-privilege is honoured by job-level scoping rather than workflow-level — the gate-evaluation steps (pip install, schema validate, ramp check, expired-config check) cannot accidentally open issues because they run in the release-gate job which has only `contents: read`. CODEOWNERS coverage on `.github/**` (per WP-SCP-020 020K) gates any change to release-gate.yml itself. The forward-compat env mirrors `SCP_REGRESSION_ASSIGNEES` from canary-replay.yml. Identified at WP-SCP-022 020H.3.1 R1 safety SAFE-MIN-003 + SAFE-MAJ-001 closures |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:86:| D-038 | 2026-05-02 | Adopt hash-pinned Python supply-chain installs across the SCP federation primitive's two YAML/JSON-validating workflows (`.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` × 4 install sites, `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` × 1 install site) via `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/policy-check.txt`. Top-level pins (`pyyaml==6.0.2` + `jsonschema==4.23.0`) match the prior inline pins exactly — no version bump on the public Python deps; only the install mechanism is hardened. Lockfile generated by `pip-compile --generate-hashes` from `requirements/policy-check.in`; full transitive closure (`attrs`, `jsonschema-specifications`, `referencing`, `rpds-py`) hash-pinned with all-platform wheel SHA256s. Closes WP-SCP-022 TF-020H3rg-002 (filed at 020H.3 R1 safety MIN-SAFE-006 — a PyPI compromise of either pinned version could substitute a malicious package on the next install; `--require-hashes` causes pip to refuse install when the served wheel's SHA256 is not in the lockfile). PATCH bump (v1.0.0 → v1.0.1) per `policies/VERSIONING.md` PATCH category (\\\"internal refactors of helpers/lib\\\"); no `policies/deprecations.yaml` entry required (no surface deprecation, no behaviour change for adopters). Lockfile regeneration command captured in `requirements/policy-check.txt` header AND `requirements/policy-check.in` documentation block | ACCEPTED | Symmetric supply-chain hardening with the pre-existing `scripts/scp-policy-check.lock` (OPA + Conftest + Regal binary SHA256 verification) and Sigstore attestation soft-warn for OPA (TF-007). All three layers — Python deps, OPA-family binaries, GitHub Actions SHA pins — are now hash-anchored at SCP source. The lockfile + `.in` source pair mirrors `scripts/.tool-versions` + `scripts/scp-policy-check.lock` (input + lockfile pattern). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged for lockfile regeneration: an operator who regenerates without re-reviewing the pip-compile output could introduce drifted transitive versions; mitigation is the `requirements/policy-check.in` source-of-truth (pins only the top-level deps; transitive resolution is automatic but reviewable in the diff). Future upgrades to `pyyaml` / `jsonschema` itself follow the same path: edit `.in`, regenerate `.txt`, review diff. The Sigstore re-tightening (TF-007) is parallel work on a different supply-chain dimension. Identified at 020H.3 R1 safety MIN-SAFE-006 closure |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:87:| D-039 | 2026-05-02 | Extend the slice 020M hash-pinned Python supply-chain install pattern to the SCP-self conflict-gate workflow (`.github/workflows/conflict-gate.yml` \\\"Install Python dependencies\\\" step) per WP-SCP-022 slice 020N, closing TF-020M-001. New `requirements/conflict-gate.in` (top-level pins matching `pyproject.toml` `[project.dependencies]` + `[project.optional-dependencies.dev]`: fastapi, uvicorn, httpx, jsonschema, pydantic, pyyaml, pytest, ruff, mypy) + generated `requirements/conflict-gate.txt` (pip-compile --generate-hashes under Python 3.12 to match `setup-python: python-version: \\\"3.12\\\"`; full transitive closure with all-platform wheel SHA256s). Install pattern: (i) `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/conflict-gate.txt` (PyPI deps); (ii) `pip install --no-deps vendor/python/ct_auth-0.8.0-py3-none-any.whl` (local vendored wheel — not on PyPI; CODEOWNERS-protected via `vendor/** @jrnb2024`); (iii) `pip install --no-deps -e .` (editable local SCP package without re-resolving deps already hash-verified in step (i)); (iv) post-install version-pin assertion (`assert yaml.__version__ == \\\"6.0.3\\\"; assert jsonschema.__version__ == \\\"4.26.0\\\"; assert fastapi.__version__ == \\\"0.136.1\\\"; assert pydantic.VERSION == \\\"2.13.3\\\"`) defending against future-PR drift (mirrors 020M SAFE-MAJ-002 pattern). Deliberate pyyaml-version drift accepted: conflict-gate.txt resolves pyyaml==6.0.3, policy-check.txt pins pyyaml==6.0.2 — independent workflows with independent supply-chain anchors; both hash-anchored. **No semver bump.** Per `policies/VERSIONING.md` §\\\"Scope\\\", `conflict-gate.yml` is not in the public-surface enumeration (workflow_call inputs on `policy-check.yml`, schema contracts, rule IDs); it is a SCP-self-only workflow that adopters do not consume. Therefore no `policies/deprecations.yaml` entry, no version-manifest bump, no release notes — internal hardening | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-038 (slice 020M hash-pinning of policy-check.yml + release-gate.yml). The conflict-gate is the third Python-installing workflow in the SCP repo; closing the unhardened install completes the Python supply-chain hardening across all three SCP-self workflows that pip-install at runtime. Threat surface (PyPI compromise of conflict-gate's deps) was acknowledged at 020M R1 safety as MIN-class because conflict-gate is SCP-self-only (not adopter-facing); a compromise would degrade SCP self's policy-evaluator quality but not directly compromise adopters. The user's directive to clear all outstanding TFs (rather than defer to v1.1 maintenance) raised this from forward-compat to in-flight closure. The `--no-deps` editable install of the local SCP package is the tradeoff: pip refuses `--require-hashes` on editable installs, so the local source tree is installed without re-resolving (its PyPI deps are already hash-verified above). The `ct-auth` vendored wheel is similarly outside `--require-hashes` (pip refuses for local file: URLs); chain-of-trust is the `vendor/**` CODEOWNERS coverage + the wheel being in-tree (no network fetch). Identified at 020M R1 safety SAFE-MIN-003 closure |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:88:| D-040 | 2026-05-02 | Amend the rule-RFC process (`docs/reviews/rule-proposals/README.md` §Process step 2) so that the 48h wall-clock review window is a CEILING (auto-defer trigger) rather than a FLOOR (minimum wait time) **in single-operator mode** (D-031 default at v1.0.0). Rationale: in single-operator mode the proposal author IS the only `SCP-CODEOWNERS` member; there are no external reviewers for the wall-clock pause to enable. The recursive 3-lens R1/R2 adversarial review (per `feedback_recursive_adversarial_review.md`) IS the adversarial-review surface; the wall-clock pause was vestigial theatre that produced no additional safety. The operator MAY merge a proposal as soon as adversarial review reaches fixpoint (no new CRIT/MAJ on a complete cycle) AND the proposal PR is open with the `scp-rule-proposal` label applied. The 48h CEILING remains in force: zero approvals by 48h still triggers auto-defer (`defer` label per slice 020L label-provisioning). When a second maintainer onboards (D-031 escalation, 2026-07-21 review), the 48h becomes a mandatory MINIMUM to give the second maintainer time to review — the CEILING-not-FLOOR posture is single-operator-only. Bypass-introducing proposals (`Bypass-surface non-empty: true`) retain their non-waivable 48h MINIMUM regardless of operator-count posture, because the additional adversarial-review value of a wall-clock pause IS material when a new bypass surface is being introduced (the operator may catch their own bypass-introducing PR's flaws on second look more reliably than for a non-bypass additive rule). Surfaced by 020L dogfood (the first RFC actually walked through the process). Closes WP-SCP-022 020L post-R2 process-gap | ACCEPTED | The 020L dogfood surfaced this gap operationally: the operator (single-maintainer) reached R1+R2 fixpoint on a non-bypass proposal and was about to wait 48h before merging — at which point the wait was identified as theatre rather than safety (no second pair of eyes to chime in). Theatre-vs-safety is the doctrine question the dogfood is designed to surface cheaply. The amendment narrows the discretionary posture to single-operator + non-bypass + post-fixpoint, leaving every other shape of the 48h window unchanged: bypass-introducing proposals keep the non-waivable minimum (the threat-surface justifies the wait); the post-2nd-maintainer-onboard 48h becomes mandatory minimum so the second maintainer has time to review; the 48h CEILING for auto-defer remains so abandoned proposals are surfaced. Symmetric with D-033's \\\"operational reality must amend the spec when the spec encounters a constraint that wasn't anticipated\\\" pattern. Identified at WP-SCP-022 slice 020L post-R2 fixpoint by operator (`@jrnb2024`) when reviewing the merge-readiness of PR #89 |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:89:| D-041 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard data shape (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1) + opt-in adopter participation model per WP-SCP-023 023B (this PR). The schema defines aggregated per-rule counts (raw_findings, denies, waived, rule_config_disabled), waivers aggregate (active_count, by_rule_id, expiring_within_30d), rule-config aggregate (disabled_rules, expiring_within_30d), repo / ref / commit / scp_version / RFC3339 emitted_at, and a verdict (allow/deny/warn). The schema EXPLICITLY DOES NOT include waiver content (`reason`, `approved_by`, `waiver_id` strings) — invariant 2 of WP-SCP-023 plan-doc binds this. The reusable workflow gains a `scorecard-emit: bool` `workflow_call` input (default false) so existing adopters see no behaviour change; opt-in adopters set `with: scorecard-emit: true`. Schema versioning: MAJOR-pinned per `policies/VERSIONING.md` D-036 + WP-SCP-023 plan-doc §10 Q1 — aggregator drops emits with unknown `schema_version`. Verification: GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation (OIDC-based) via `actions/attest-build-provenance@v4.1.0` (SHA `a2bbfa25...`) at emit time; aggregator verifies via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow` (per D-042 to be filed at slice 023C). v1.2.0 cut on this slice's merge per VERSIONING.md MINOR category | ACCEPTED | This is the first slice of WP-SCP-023's implementation chain (023A plan-doc landed at PR #97, commit `7075234`, 2026-05-03 R4 fixpoint). The data shape was specified at plan-doc level; this slice ratifies it as code surface. Default-false on the workflow input is the load-bearing safety property: existing adopters cannot have new behaviour spring on them; opt-in is explicit per invariant 4. The waiver-content exclusion (invariant 2) is enforced by the schema's `additionalProperties: false` constraint on every level + the explicit field enumeration. The MAJOR-pinning posture means schema breakage requires v2.0.0 + adopter migration; v0.1 prefix on `schema_version` reflects the freedom to amend until first adopter opts in. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-041 reservation |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:90:| D-042 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard aggregator pipeline trust model per WP-SCP-023 023C (this PR). Mechanism: per-emit verification via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow <expected_workflow_ref>` (the GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation OIDC pattern, mandatory per the D-042 reservation note above + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure); index trust rooted in git's required-signed-commits (slice 020J) + `output/scorecards/** @jrnb2024` CODEOWNERS coverage (slice 023A) + branch protection on main (slice 020D2), NOT a separate Ed25519 key layer. The aggregator runs as `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` on a weekly cron (Monday 06:00 UTC) + `workflow_dispatch`; two-job structure (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped via job-level permissions, mirroring the 023B `attest-scorecard` job split); reads `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml` (CODEOWNERS-protected at `docs/scorecards/**`), pulls each adopter's latest green policy-check run's `scorecard-emit.json` artifact, verifies attestation, schema-validates emit, aggregates into `output/scorecards/index.json` (schema: `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`), and opens a PR for operator review. Failure modes (verification_failure / unreachable / no_emit) record loudly per-adopter — never silently dropped. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema `additionalProperties: false` at every level). Internal-only workflow per `policies/VERSIONING.md` §\\\"Scope\\\" (mirrors 020N conflict-gate.yml posture); no semver bump. Verifies WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 6 (\\\"Aggregator output is Ed25519-signed\\\") in spirit — Sigstore/Fulcio uses Ed25519 under the hood, managed by GitHub rather than by an SCP-side private key, eliminating the private-key-distribution surface | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 (per-emit data shape + opt-in model) — D-041 ratified the EMITTER side of the trust model; D-042 ratifies the AGGREGATOR / VERIFIER side. The mandatory `--signer-workflow` constraint was already pre-committed at the D-042 reservation note above (closes 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001) — this slice ratifies it as workflow code. The Ed25519-via-Sigstore framing eliminates the chicken-and-egg of \\\"where does the SCP private key live and how does the aggregator hold it without exposing adopters\\\" — GitHub manages the keys via OIDC + Sigstore. The two-job permission split (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped) is identical to 023B's `policy-check` + `attest-scorecard` split (closes the analogous threat surface where workflow-level write permissions could be exploited by a compromised aggregate-side step). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-042 reservation + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:91:| D-043 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report (`docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`) + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` — per WP-SCP-023 023D (this PR). Markdown generator at `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` produces deterministic golden-file-tested output reading `output/scorecards/index.json`; aggregator workflow `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` extended in the commit job to invoke the generator + add the rendered markdown to the operator-review PR alongside the index. MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` (registered in `src/standards_control_plane/mcp_server/tools.py`): read-only contract per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 5; request shape `{repo_filter?, since_emitted_at?}`; response shape excludes waiver content (`reason` / `approved_by` / `waiver_id` — invariant 2) by Pydantic model construction (extra=forbid + explicit field whitelist). The MCP method reads `output/scorecards/index.json` from the SCP repo working copy at call time; staleness is observable via the response's `aggregated_at` field. ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 documents the adopter onboarding workflow. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by Pydantic models + schema + dedicated pytest scans on both markdown + MCP responses) | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 + D-042 — D-043 ratifies the CONSUMER side: markdown for operators/auditors, MCP for agents/tooling. Read-only contract + Pydantic-enforced field whitelist + golden-file pytest together preserve invariant 2 across both surfaces. The MCP method does NOT introduce a new authentication primitive — it rides on WP-SCP-021's existing Ed25519 receipt mechanism (consult-class semantics). The markdown report is informational and CODEOWNERS-protected via `docs/scorecards/** @jrnb2024`; operators can hand-edit before merging the aggregator PR if needed (regenerator overwrites on next run). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the MCP server runs at acc.brokapps.ai; if down, agents lose `consult_scorecard` access but the markdown report + git index remain consultable. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-043 reservation |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:92:| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-core operational contracts for cascade scaffolding. Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (`SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically - bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits a TF-023E-002 warning for post-v1.2.0 SHAs while recommending the v1.0.0 pin; `--scp-sha` 40-char hex regex; `--default-branch` enum {main, master, develop}; `--scorecard-emit` enum; `--output-dir` writability + path-normalised system-path denylist (incl `/private/var/*` macOS canonicalisation); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments per plan-doc §5.3. Canonical adopter slugs are normalization aids only, not collision-resistant IDs, so cohort repo names must remain unique after canonicalization. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12 with Renovate inline-comment marker `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-` enabling auto-bump per plan-doc invariant 8 Threshold A criterion; substitutions `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`, `{{SCP_SHA}}`, `{{SCORECARD_EMIT}}`; least-privilege workflow-level permissions (`contents:read` + `statuses:write` only). (3) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CLI tool implements plan-doc invariant 2 cascade-status CI enforcement: 4 enforcement behaviours (fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised; `onboarded` -> log-entry-modified + target-match; `onboarded-operator-bump` -> log entry + `STATUS.md` `TF-024X-renovate-<slug>` row matching invariant 2 regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` -> `DISPATCH-NOTE` `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference + log file NOT modified) + explicit tooling-slice opt-in gate for `cascade-status: not applicable` (`--allow-not-applicable`; default refusal for direct CLI use). Regex via `python3 re.search()` (PCRE-style); exactly-one-match assertions on both `cascade-status` and `**Target:**` extraction close multi-occurrence injection bypasses; adopter-slug canonicalisation per plan-doc spec. CLI tool only - GitHub Actions workflow wiring (`.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`) defers to slice 024B-extras alongside `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure. D-044 was reserved for slice 024B at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04); after the operator-decided scope-split (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md), D-044 stays scoped to core deliverables; sibling D-NNN may be reserved at 024B-extras authoring time for the deferred surface (`--restore` + break-glass + workflow wiring). Slice 024B-core ships under documented protocol deviation per feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md note + justify rule (kernel hook lives in ACC repo only; per-repo install pattern is FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 - open). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge per the §9 reservation block. The original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds against a single branch with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code (R6 missed primary-deliverable workflow wiring; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR). Empirical signal: surface area too large (16 files, ~3500 lines added) for single-pass convergence. Operator decided 2026-05-09 to split 024B into 024B-core (this slice; ~5 files; scaffolder + template + CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (deferred; `--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope - both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens. Original 024B work preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` branch (audit trail: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log files + 7 R-round archive directories incl r8-archive carry-forward findings). Slice 024B-core scope is internally coherent: scaffolder generates adopter artefacts; CI enforcement script (CLI) validates cascade-status declarations; tests cover both. The CLI script can be invoked manually as a stop-gap until 024B-extras wires it into GitHub Actions. The CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient: workflow-side hardcoding of `--tooling-slice-id` and omission of `--allow-not-applicable` in 024B-extras is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation |\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:93:| D-047 | 2026-05-10 | Adopt WP-SCP-024 024B-extras operational contracts: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` restores branch protection from the captured prior-state log entry by transforming GET-shape JSON into the PUT body, stripping envelope fields recursively, converting `enforce_admins.enabled` to a boolean, and replaying `required_signatures` through the dedicated sub-resource; restore-mode posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement` and `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks` are mandatory when the target removes those protections; forward-mode now performs a path-pinned workflow lookup for `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`, queries workflow-runs without a branch filter, validates `--expected-wrapper-sha` against actual release tags via `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/git/ref/tags/<tag>`, and treats the working-tree diff of `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` as part of prior-entry detection; the new CI workflow `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires the CLI gate into PR checks with `paths-ignore: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**`; ADOPT-001 gains §12.8 break-glass procedure; STATUS.md and the DISPATCH-NOTE placeholder for the step-7 operator demo are updated in-slice. | ACCEPTED | The 024B split left the restore / break-glass / workflow-integration surface as the deferred half so the review load stayed bounded. This decision ratifies the operational contract that lets operators disable and re-enable the federation primitive safely without widening the adopter-facing API surface, while preserving the bootstrap guard that prevents tooling slices from self-blocking their own PRs. The release-tag SHA requirement is intentionally anchored to actual git tags, not arbitrary commits, so Gate 3 can re-arm against a concrete release artifact rather than against moving main-head. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, and the restore demo evidence is still an operator-interactive step outside Codex dispatch. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras authoring time. | \\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:94:\\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:95:> D-044 limitation note: the CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient. 024B-extras must hardcode `--tooling-slice-id` per workflow file and omit `--allow-not-applicable` from cohort workflows; that workflow-side hardcoding is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001).\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:1:#!/usr/bin/env bash\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:2:# shellcheck shell=bash\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:3:# WP-SCP-020 slice 020G — adopter-side branch-protection helper.\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:4:#\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:5:# Configures a downstream adopter repo's default branch with the\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:6:# canonical SCP federation primitive required-status-check posture:\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:7:#\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:8:#   - required_status_checks.contexts = [\\\"${SCP_REQUIRED_CONTEXT}\\\"]\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:9:#     (default: \\\"policy-check / scp/policy-check\\\" — the rendered\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:10:#     check-run name from the canonical adopter wrapper)\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:11:#   - required_status_checks.strict = true (PR must be up-to-date\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:12:#     with base before evaluation)\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:13:#   - enforce_admins = true (no admin bypass)\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:14:#   - required_signatures = true (every commit verified-signed,\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:15:#     applied via dedicated sub-resource endpoint)\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:16:#\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:17:# This is the adopter-side analogue of SCP-self's\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:18:# `scripts/configure-020d2-required-check.sh`. Adopters with\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:19:# multi-maintainer teams MAY enable additional review gates;\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:20:# the script preserves any existing required_pull_request_reviews\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:21:# rather than nulling them out (per 020G R1 SAF-002 closure).\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:22:#\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:23:# ## Bootstrap-only — NOT run unattended\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:24:#\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:25:# This script writes durable state to a third-party repository\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:26:# (the adopter's branch protection). It refuses to run when CI=true\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:27:# or GITHUB_ACTIONS=true (the two standard CI env vars). Operator\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:28:# attention is required to:\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:29:#   - confirm the target via --plan first\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:30:#   - review the diff between before-state and after-state\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:31:#   - paste the emitted markdown log entry into the SCP repo's\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:32:#     `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` and merge.\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:33:#\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:34:# The log commit is part of the invocation procedure per\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:35:# WP-SCP-020 §4 020G(iii). The script emits a log block on EVERY\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:36:# completed invocation, including verification failures and partial-\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:37:# state apply failures (e.g. the unified PUT succeeds but the\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:38:# required_signatures POST fails) — the operator commits the\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:39:# resulting log entry whether the apply succeeded or partially\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:40:# failed, so the audit trail captures both outcomes.\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:41:#\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:42:# ## Required PAT scope\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:43:#\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:44:# `gh` must be authenticated with `administration:write` on the\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:45:# target repo (fine-grained PAT with single-repo scope strongly\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:46:# preferred over classic). The script cannot introspect token\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:47:# scope without making an authorised call; on the first PUT it\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:48:# will fail with HTTP 403 if the scope is insufficient. Run with\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:49:# `--plan` first to verify intent before any mutation.\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:50:#\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:51:# Reference: docs/DECISIONS.md D-022 (federation-primitive adoption);\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:52:# D-033 (the rendered context name `policy-check / scp/policy-check`\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:53:# established for the SCP self-dogfood gate, used here as the\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:54:# canonical adopter default); D-035 (this slice's invocation\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:55:# procedure); WP-SCP-020 §4 020G; ADOPT-001 §12 (federation\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:56:# integration appendix — lands in 020H part 3).\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:57:\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:58:set -euo pipefail\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:59:\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:60:# ---------- Bootstrap-only guard ----------\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:61:\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:62:if [ \\\"${CI:-}\\\" = \\\"true\\\" ] || [ \\\"${GITHUB_ACTIONS:-}\\\" = \\\"true\\\" ]; then\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:63:  echo \\\"020G refuses to run in CI: this is an attended bootstrap script.\\\" >&2\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:64:  echo \\\"If you need to run a dry-run from CI, unset CI/GITHUB_ACTIONS first AND pass --plan explicitly.\\\" >&2\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:65:  exit 1\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:66:fi\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:67:\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:68:# ---------- (i) Header preconditions ----------\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:69:\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:70:require_cmd() {\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:71:  command -v \\\"$1\\\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || {\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:72:    echo \\\"missing required command: $1\\\" >&2\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:73:    exit 1\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:74:  }\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:75:}\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:76:\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:77:require_cmd gh\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:78:require_cmd jq\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:79:require_cmd git\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:80:require_cmd python3\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:81:require_cmd shasum\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:82:\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:83:assert_gh_version() {\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:84:  local raw major minor\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:85:  raw=\\\"$(gh --version 2>/dev/null | head -1 | awk '{print $3}')\\\"\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:86:  if [ -z \\\"$raw\\\" ]; then\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:87:    echo \\\"could not determine gh CLI version\\\" >&2\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:88:    exit 1\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:89:  fi\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:90:  major=\\\"$(printf '%s' \\\"$raw\\\" | cut -d. -f1)\\\"\\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:91:  minor=\\\"$(printf '%s' \\\"$raw\\\" | cut -d. -f2)\\\"\\nscripts/enable-r