**020Q** | Conflict-gate suppression-path corpus + Python waiver-awareness (closes TF-006). New helpers in `tests/conflict_gate/test_conflict_gate.py` mirror `policies/scp_common.rego` 1:1 (`_parse_dateish_ns`, `_scp_waiver_expired`, `_scp_active_waiver_for`, `_scp_rule_config_disabled`). `_run_opa` plumbs sibling `waivers.json` + `.scp/rule-config.yaml` through `--data` tempfile. 6 new fixtures (waiver-suppressed × 3 rules, waiver-expired, rule-config-disabled, waiver-null-expires-at). 12/12 pass; both engines agree on every code path. R1 surfaced + closed a real silent-bypass bug in `scp_common.rego` (null `expires_at` → undefined → suppression falsely active); fixed by an explicit fail-closed clause. CI fixpoint #1: skip `tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/**` from production conftest target list (latent bug exposed by adding 6 new fixtures simultaneously). Merged at `974a173`. **Unblocks WP-SCP-023.** |\\n\\n## Today's chain (2026-05-03 — WP-SCP-023 closed at Threshold A scaffolding + WP-SCP-024 opens)\\n\\n| # | PR | Slice | Outcome |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | #97 | **023A** | WP-SCP-023 plan-doc v0.1 — cross-repo scorecards. Defines per-repo emit contract, central aggregator, exposure surface (markdown + MCP), Threshold A criterion (≥3 adopters opted in + weekly aggregator + USER-GATE-D). Reserves D-041/D-042/D-043 for implementation slices 023B/C/D (D-042 mandatory `job_workflow_ref` constraint per `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow`). Move #5 of the 5-move MVCP — estate-wide observability for the federation primitive. R4 fixpoint reached after 4-round adversarial review (1 CRIT + 7 unique MAJ + 7 MIN closed across rounds). Merged at `7075234`. |\\n| 2 | #98 | **023B** | Per-repo scorecard emitter + schema (closes D-041). NEW `schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1 (MAJOR-pinned per VERSIONING.md D-036). NEW opt-in `scorecard-emit: bool` workflow_call input on `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` (default false; existing adopters see no behaviour change). New separate `attest-scorecard` job with job-scoped OIDC permissions (closes 023B R1 MAJ-SAFE-001 — workflow-level `id-token: write` would have exposed adopter cloud-IAM trust to ALL runs). 4 fixture pairs (minimal / full / deny-with-waiver / warn-baseline); 12/12 pytest pass. NEVER emits waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema + dedicated pytest scan). v1.1.0 → **v1.2.0** (MINOR per VERSIONING.md additive-opt-in). 3-round adversarial review caught 6 unique MAJs. Merged at `5d4341b`; `v1.2.0` tag cut + GitHub release published; release-gate dry-run + post-tag observer both clean. |\\n| 3 | #99 | **023C** | Cross-repo aggregator workflow + central index + opt-in registry (closes D-042). NEW `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` (weekly cron + workflow_dispatch; two-job permission scoping — aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped; staleness check; prior-row retention). NEW `schemas/scorecard-opt-in-registry.schema.json` + `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json` (regex anchored to SCP namespace; allOf if/then conditional branches). NEW `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml` + `output/scorecards/index.json` placeholder + `output/scorecards/README.md`. 2-round adversarial review caught 4 unique MAJs (signer-workflow regex defence-in-depth; conditional schema branches; status enum description mismatch; missing 7-day staleness check). Merged at `47f7f0c`. |\\n| 4 | #100 | **023D** | Cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` (closes D-043). NEW `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` (deterministic golden-file-tested output; reads `output/scorecards/index.json` → `docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`). Aggregator workflow extended (commit job invokes generator + adds markdown to operator-review PR). NEW MCP method `consult_scorecard` in `src/standards_control_plane/mcp_server/tools.py` with read-only contract per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 5 (request: `repo_filter?` + `since_emitted_at?`; response: aggregated counts only, NEVER waiver content per invariant 2). NEW `tests/scorecard-report/` (3 golden fixtures × 2 tests = 7) + `tests/scp_mcp/test_tools/test_consult_scorecard.py` (9 tests including waiver-content scan). NEW ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 — adopter onboarding workflow (opt-in PR, privacy contract, MCP usage, 4 common failure modes table). 51/51 pytest pass. Internal-only delta to aggregator workflow; MCP method addition is additive (registered tool name only) so no federation primitive version bump per VERSIONING.md §\\\"Scope\\\". |\\n| 5 | #101 | **023E** | WP-SCP-023 Threshold A scaffolding (closes TF-023D-003 + TF-023A-002; **defers TF-023C-001 → TF-023E-001 + TF-023E-002**). NEW `docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md` (status: `not-yet-signed`) — 8-criterion checklist for operator sign-off when ≥3 adopters (FLA mandatory) opted in + first weekly aggregator clean. Closed TF-023D-003: `_log_tool_invocation` now reads active key_id from `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` via new `_resolve_audit_key_id()` helper (graceful fallback `key-ring-unreadable` if key ring empty/malformed; never blocks tool calls). Updated `test_stdio_handshake.py` expected tools list to include `consult_scorecard`. 86/86 MCP tests pass. **fix-round-3:** Two real CI gaps surfaced — (1) SCP-self opt-in attempted then reverted because GitHub blocks `actions/attest-build-provenance` on user-owned private repos (filed TF-023E-001). (2) Wrapper SHA pin bump (v1.0.0 → @5ff2acd) reverted because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation), and the `attest-scorecard` job's `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` exceed the wrapper's ceiling — startup_failure even with `scorecard-emit: false` (filed TF-023E-002 — restructure policy-check.yml so attest-scorecard is a separate top-level workflow file). USER-GATE-D criterion (i) updated: SCP-self carve-out — satisfied set is now `FLA + ≥2 of {PIM / recommender / mapp-doc-agent / control-tower}`