W opt-in `scorecard-emit: bool` workflow_call input on `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` (default false; existing adopters see no behaviour change). New separate `attest-scorecard` job with job-scoped OIDC permissions (closes 023B R1 MAJ-SAFE-001 — workflow-level `id-token: write` would have exposed adopter cloud-IAM trust to ALL runs). 4 fixture pairs (minimal / full / deny-with-waiver / warn-baseline); 12/12 pytest pass. NEVER emits waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema + dedicated pytest scan). v1.1.0 → **v1.2.0** (MINOR per VERSIONING.md additive-opt-in). 3-round adversarial review caught 6 unique MAJs. Merged at `5d4341b`; `v1.2.0` tag cut + GitHub release published; release-gate dry-run + post-tag observer both clean. |\\n| 3 | #99 | **023C** | Cross-repo aggregator workflow + central index + opt-in registry (closes D-042). NEW `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` (weekly cron + workflow_dispatch; two-job permission scoping — aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped; staleness check; prior-row retention). NEW `schemas/scorecard-opt-in-registry.schema.json` + `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json` (regex anchored to SCP namespace; allOf if/then conditional branches). NEW `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml` + `output/scorecards/index.json` placeholder + `output/scorecards/README.md`. 2-round adversarial review caught 4 unique MAJs (signer-workflow regex defence-in-depth; conditional schema branches; status enum description mismatch; missing 7-day staleness check). Merged at `47f7f0c`. |\\n| 4 | #100 | **023D** | Cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` (closes D-043). NEW `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` (deterministic golden-file-tested output; reads `output/scorecards/index.json` → `docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`). Aggregator workflow extended (commit job invokes generator + adds markdown to operator-review PR). NEW MCP method `consult_scorecard` in `src/standards_control_plane/mcp_server/tools.py` with read-only contract per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 5 (request: `repo_filter?` + `since_emitted_at?`; response: aggregated counts only, NEVER waiver content per invariant 2). NEW `tests/scorecard-report/` (3 golden fixtures × 2 tests = 7) + `tests/scp_mcp/test_tools/test_consult_scorecard.py` (9 tests including waiver-content scan). NEW ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 — adopter onboarding workflow (opt-in PR, privacy contract, MCP usage, 4 common failure modes table). 51/51 pytest pass. Internal-only delta to aggregator workflow; MCP method addition is additive (registered tool name only) so no federation primitive version bump per VERSIONING.md §\\\"Scope\\\". |\\n| 5 | #101 | **023E** | WP-SCP-023 Threshold A scaffolding (closes TF-023D-003 + TF-023A-002; **defers TF-023C-001 → TF-023E-001 + TF-023E-002**). NEW `docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md` (status: `not-yet-signed`) — 8-criterion checklist for operator sign-off when ≥3 adopters (FLA mandatory) opted in + first weekly aggregator clean. Closed TF-023D-003: `_log_tool_invocation` now reads active key_id from `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` via new `_resolve_audit_key_id()` helper (graceful fallback `key-ring-unreadable` if key ring empty/malformed; never blocks tool calls). Updated `test_stdio_handshake.py` expected tools list to include `consult_scorecard`. 86/86 MCP tests pass. **fix-round-3:** Two real CI gaps surfaced — (1) SCP-self opt-in attempted then reverted because GitHub blocks `actions/attest-build-provenance` on user-owned private repos (filed TF-023E-001). (2) Wrapper SHA pin bump (v1.0.0 → @5ff2acd) reverted because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation), and the `attest-scorecard` job's `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` exceed the wrapper's ceiling — startup_failure even with `scorecard-emit: false` (filed TF-023E-002 — restructure policy-check.yml so attest-scorecard is a separate top-level workflow