. The integation appendix is scheduled for 020H part 3, a downstream slice.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Any reader (human or agent) following the ADOPT-001 \\u00a712 pointer today finds general architecture principles, not the federation integration guide. Governance audit trail is weakened: cited conformance reference does not yet exist in the cited document at the expected content. Forward references in governance-sensitive workflow headers are a completeness gap per the no-silent-descope invariant.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Amend wrapper header to annotate the forward reference: change '(ADOPT-001 \\u00a712)' to '(ADOPT-001 \\u00a712, federation integration appendix \\u2014 pending 020H part 3 publication)'. This is a one-line comment change that closes the misleading pointer before it propagates.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"COMP-NIT-001\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"nit\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"WP-SCP-020 \\u00a74 020D1 spec text '@<commit-SHA-of-v1.0.0-rc.1>' is timing-ambiguous: the tag is cut after 020D1 merges, not before\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"WP-SCP-020 \\u00a74 020D1: 'SCP's own repo adds policy-check-wrapper.yml calling the reusable workflow at @<commit-SHA-of-v1.0.0-rc.1>.' 020H part 1 (immediately downstream): 'Cut v1.0.0-rc.1 tag from the 020D1 merge commit.' The wrapper correctly pins at `9820489fa83f64d04f641d20e99d3933cefbb04a` (020K merge SHA, latest main at PR-open). Dispatch note and wrapper comments document the ratchet lifecycle (020D1 pins 020K SHA \\u2192 020H.1 cuts tag \\u2192 020D1.1 ratchets pin). The implementation is correct; the spec phrasing is ambiguous.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"A future reader of the 020D1 spec row could interpret '@<commit-SHA-of-v1.0.0-rc.1>' as requiring the v1.0.0-rc.1 SHA to be known at PR-open time, which is temporally impossible since the tag is cut from the merge commit. Ambiguity about the 020D1 vs 020D1.1 ratchet split.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Amend WP-SCP-020 \\u00a74 020D1 spec text to: 'calling the reusable workflow at @<most-recent-main-SHA at PR-open time>; pin ratcheted to v1.0.0-rc.1 SHA in follow-up slice 020D1.1.' Non-blocking for 020D1 merge.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"COMP-NIT-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"nit\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"docs/reviews/** path is not covered by CODEOWNERS; governance evidence artifacts are modifiable without mandatory CODEOWNER review signal\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CODEOWNERS covers: policies/**, schemas/**, lib/**, .github/**, tests/**, renovate/**, docs/DECISIONS.md, docs/security/**, docs/adoption/**, docs/plans/**, docs/integrations/**, output/findings/**, output/control-tower/**, output/ci/**, /CODEOWNERS, docs/CODEOWNERS. No entry for docs/reviews/**. 020K R1+R2 review closed 7 MAJ + 4 MIN findings by extending coverage; docs/reviews/ was not added. Dispatch evidence dir docs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020d1/ holds R1 review JSON outputs.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"impact\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"In a multi-maintainer future, review evidence artifacts (dispatch notes, R1 review JSON) could be added or modified in a PR without triggering CODEOWNER review request. In current solo-operator model this is moot. The gap will compound when a second maintainer onboards: per 020K, at that point CODEOWNERS coverage should already be comprehensive and a retroactive fix may be missed.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mitigation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Add `docs/reviews/** @jrnb2024` to CODEOWNERS in this PR or at the quarterly bus-factor-1 escalation review (2026-07-21). Alternatively, add an explicit exclusion note in the CODEOWNERS header explaining why docs/reviews/ is intentionally not covered. Non-blocking for 020D1.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Slice 020D1 is structurally sound: wrapper exists at the correct path, 40-char SHA pin `9820489fa83f64d04f641d20e99d3933cefbb04a` matches the 020K merge commit in main history, advisory-mode assertion is accurate, fork PR refusal is implemented, permissions are `contents: read, statuses: write` per D-029, no `secrets:` block, pin lifecycle is clearly documented in wrapper header and dispatch note, risk profile correctly marked HIGH with CI fixpoint categories enumerated, and the slice is a pure additive change (wrapper + dispatch evidence dir only). One MAJ finding (plan canonical template wrong repo name \\u2014 no trailing dash) is a pre-existing spec doc defect that must be resolved before 020H part 3 publication but does not block 020D1 merge. Two MIN findings (fork PR refusal AC gap in canonical example; ADOPT-001 \\u00a712 forward reference unannotated) require resolution before 020H part 3 lands. Two nit findings (spec text timing ambiguity; docs/reviews CODEOWNERS gap) are non-blocking. Conditional pass: merge proceeds; MAJ-001 and both MIN findings are tracked forward as obligations on 020H part 3 authorship.\\\\\\\"}\\\",\\\"stop_reason\\\":\\\"end_turn\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"a1863ac3-3e43-4929-bac8-cf96367eabe3\\\",\\\"total_cost_usd\\\":0.4984297,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2349,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":41654,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":154194,\\\"output_tokens\\\":19156,\\\"server_tool_use\\\":{\\\"web_search_requests\\\":0,\\\"web_fetch_requests\\\":0},\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":41654,\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0},\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"iterations\\\":[{\\\"input_tokens\\\":1,\\\"output_tokens\\\":18021,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":47538,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":1987,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":1987},\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\"}],\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"modelUsage\\\":{\\\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":1447,\\\"outputTokens\\\":27,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":0,\\\"cacheCre